{"parentUuid":"58008035-223a-4b20-87f9-9c486c9b8f01","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dfa17e39-886f-43de-a827-ca753f33b2a4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nThe user is building **Fitcheck**, a Next.js 16 / Supabase mobile wardrobe app (generator picks daily outfits). This session covered: finishing the generator plan (material matrix, frame/rule registry), shipping 0.2.0 to production, a large product/ops roadmap, legal pages, CI, the background-removal rebuild, and now a **model bake-off**. Standing intents:\n\n- **Quality over cleverness for the generator**; encode research; build for N users, never the user's own closet.\n- **Process rules from the user (verbatim where important):**\n  - *\"next time, just give me commands to make a pull request and text for it\"* — later overridden by *\"bro, can u do it all, im lost\"* for the release flow, but then: *\"did u made a full review of that function, dont merge without my permission\"* → **never merge a PR without an explicit go** (saved to memory `no-merge-without-permission.md`).\n  - *\"after whole implementation of that make full branch review\"* — mutation-sweep every branch before commit/push; user later complained *\"u forgot to make branch review before commit and push\"*.\n  - *\"make less text in our chat\"* but *\"if its really important disscusion etc, read with me a lot\"*.\n  - *\"dont look on my garderobe... We are making for a huge amount of users. Also write less comments in code.\"*\n  - *\"we will do for now only manuel backups mate\"*; *\"we would do paddle but a lot later, when we would have enough revenue\"*; *\"go with amber\"* (free, clean-licence models); later *\"i dont want have questions to lawyer\"*.\n- **Security/constraints:** repo `1curafu/Fitcheck` is **PUBLIC**; `Test assets/` (user's wardrobe photos) is gitignored and must never be committed; `docs/` is gitignored (contains legal DPAs, research, plans, STATE.md); `.env.local` holds secrets (never commit); Supabase project `pbuccfnuraebpkuzjaot` (org on **free plan**, no backups); default branch is now `main`; `feat/*` → `develop` → `main` (main = Vercel prod).\n- **Most recent explicit request:** *\"wait, so just use with mit license, just test RMBG-2.0, BiRefNet and our old model, that we used, whats better, like take all models that theoreticaly works for us and test and give me comparison on photos, i will see difference\"* — a full visual comparison sheet across all candidate models on the 34 real photos.\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n- Next.js 16.3 Cache Components; `npm run insights` gate; `next start` for e2e (not dev); Turbopack cache corruption from stray `\" 2\"` duplicate files → `rm -rf .next`.\n- Supabase local (docker `supabase_db_Fitcheck`, Mailpit :54324) and production; MCP tools (`list_migrations`, `execute_sql`, `apply_migration` — classifier blocks DDL with DROP/UPDATE).\n- Additive weight budget scorer; mutation testing as review; source-level guard tests (`producers.test.ts`, `legal.test.ts`).\n- Rule registry: HARD/STRONG/PREFERENCE/CONTESTED with relief valve (`relieve`), HARD rules carry a relief weight.\n- Background removal: `onnxruntime-web/wasm` (lazy import to avoid SSR \"Invalid URL\"), u2netp (Apache-2.0, DUTS, exported by us with dynamic axes, sha256 `d6811788…`, 4.64 MB), IoU parity harness against `@imgly` baselines with reference overrides; `useSyncExternalStore` for localStorage.\n- Stripe: hosted Checkout, flat-rate monthly + annual (EUR), Customer Portal cancel; Swiss account; bank via Yuh Pro; statement descriptor `FITCHECK.SPACE`.\n- Legal: FADP + GDPR; policy-as-data; cookie notice (strictly necessary only); Sentry replay off; Vercel Analytics (cookieless).\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections (most important)\n\n- `lib/generator/styling/material-matrix.ts`, `frame.ts`, `styling/registry.ts` (RULES: sneaker-at-formal HARD 0.5, distressed-at-formal HARD 0.5, logos-past-two STRONG 0.3, two-loud-logos STRONG 0.15, loud-logo-in-classic STRONG 0.25 classic-only, black-with-navy/brown CONTESTED; `applyRules`, `relieve`), `rank.ts` (`rankTopN` returns `Ranked<T>` with `verdict`, calls `relieve`), `rerank.ts` (`buildRerankPrompt` with \"Judgement calls\" block), `from-row.ts` (`CANDIDATE_COLUMNS`, `CANDIDATE_SELECT`, `toCandidateItem`, `stylistInputFor`), `__tests__/producers.test.ts`.\n- `lib/generator/styling/bag.ts` — `bagCoordination`: ECHO 1, BLEND 0.85, CONTRAST 0.85, PLAIN 0.8 (measured), CLUTTER 0.4; weight `bag: 0.12` in score.ts. `trios.ts` `FAMILY` now covers all 42 colours (red/green/yellow/purple/pink/teal families) with a coverage test.\n- `lib/release-notes.ts` (v0.2.0 entry), `components/shell/whats-new.tsx` (useSyncExternalStore, `shouldShow`), `whats-new-card.tsx` (collapsed with chevron), mounted in `app/closet/page.tsx`; `vitest.setup.ts` localStorage polyfill.\n- `components/closet/use-style-with-item.ts`, `components/outfits/try-another-look.tsx` (hairline pill in 2-col grid under Favourite/Wear, `col-span-2 -mt-1`); `style-cta.tsx` slimmed.\n- `lib/legal/{types,privacy,terms}.ts`, `components/legal/legal-document.tsx`, `app/privacy/page.tsx`, `app/terms/page.tsx`, `components/shell/cookie-notice.tsx` (in-flow, first child of `MobileShell`), `lib/legal/__tests__/legal.test.ts` (PROCESSORS with `says` regex per vendor), `instrumentation-client.ts` (integrations [], tracesSampleRate 0.1, dataCollection userInfo false), `app/layout.tsx` `<Analytics />`, links in `settings-view.tsx`, `app/page.tsx`, `profile-hub.tsx`, `quiz.tsx` (\"By continuing you confirm you are 16 or older and agree…\").\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — trigger now `branches: [develop, main]`, lint step added; `eslint.config.mjs` ignores `styling/**`, `public/ort/**`, `scratch/**`, `docs/**`.\n- `e2e/capture.spec.ts` (uses `e2e/fixtures/garment.jpg`, drawn synthetic shirt, `test.use({ storageState: \"e2e/.auth/state.json\" })`); `lib/ai/tag-item.ts` `stubbedTags()` (non-exported) under `FITCHECK_STUB_AI`.\n- `lib/images/segment.ts` — `SegmentModel {url,inputSize,mean,std,output?:\"probability\"|\"logits\"}`, `RefineOptions {sharpen?, guided?, zoom?{padFrac,maxAreaFrac,square?}}`, `U2NETP`, `U2NETP_REFINE = { sharpen: [0.2, 0.8] }`, lazy `ort()` with provider wasm|webgpu, `configureRuntime(paths, provider)`, `inferRegion`, `maskBounds`, `segmentMask(source, model, at?, refine)`, `segment(source, model, target=source, refine)`. `lib/images/refine.ts` (`sharpenAlpha`, `boxMean`, `guidedFilter`, `luminance`), `mask-metrics.ts`, `process.ts` (`segment(file, U2NETP, original, U2NETP_REFINE)`), `lib/images/__tests__/fixtures/parity-reference.json`, `scripts/copy-ort.mjs` (prebuild/predev), `scripts/cutout-harness/run.mjs` (flags: `--check`, `--record`, `--compressed-input`; env `REFINE`, `SIZE`, `MODEL=birefnet`, `GPU=1`, `FROM_DIR=<dir>`; reference overrides in `scratch/reference/` for 3 images), `harness.html` (importmap incl. webgpu bundle), `harness-imgly.html` (imgly + ORT 1.21 vendored in `scratch/ort121`), `next.config.ts` immutable headers for `/models|ort`, CLAUDE.md Decision 2 rewritten.\n- Scratch (local, gitignored): `scratch/export/{export.py,u2net.py,u2netp.pth,u2net.pth,birefnet.py,sam2.py,u2net_run.py,hf_seg.py}`, `scratch/candidates/{birefnet_lite,sam2_tiny,sam2_small,sam2_baseplus,u2net_full,u2_ensemble}`, `scratch/parity-*.json`, `scratch/result-sheet.mjs`, `scratch/models/birefnet_lite_fp16.onnx` (114.5 MB).\n- Docs (local): `docs/superpowers/plans/roadmap-2026-09-14.md` (the one list with statuses), `docs/legal/security-incident.md`, `docs/legal/ropa.md` (DPA checklist; user has saved 7 DPA PDFs), `docs/STATE.md`, `docs/research/fitcheck-privacy-terms-review.md` (checklist ticked).\n\n## 4. Errors and fixes\n- Confounded scorer tests (warmth) → no-climate context.\n- Plan's frame fixture inconsistent with its own `soleFormality` → used Leather+Chunky (2.5) as ambiguous.\n- Producer mappings unguarded (8 survivors) → `toCandidateItem`; last survivor → `producers.test.ts` source guard.\n- Backup basename collision in a sweep corrupted files → unique backup names; `git checkout-index` restored app files unexpectedly; background sweep racing foreground → never run two git-touching commands concurrently.\n- `git stash -u` with uncommitted `.gitignore` wiped `scratch/` twice; `git add -A` on a branch without the ignore committed 1,183 artefacts into PR #79 (merged) → cleanup PR #81; verified **no secrets leaked**. Commit the `.gitignore` first.\n- `.next` Turbopack \"Failed to open database / invalid digit\" → stray `\" N\"` files; `rm -rf .next`.\n- Stale `next start` on :3000 served old builds; kill before e2e.\n- Cookie notice fixed top covered detail-page Back button (e2e clicks timed out) → in-flow at top of shell. CI hadn't caught it because the workflow only ran for PRs into main.\n- e2e capture spec: missing `test.use({ storageState })` (20 min chasing \"redirect\"); `Test assets/` not in CI → synthetic fixture.\n- `\"use server\"` module can't export sync function → `stubbedTags` non-exported.\n- `@imgly` doesn't declare onnxruntime-web; installing ORT 1.30 broke it (`_OrtGetInputOutputMetadata`) → vendored 1.21 + imgly in `scratch/ort121` for baselines.\n- ORT default bundle wants JSEP → `onnxruntime-web/wasm` entry; module-scope `import.meta.url` → SSR \"Invalid URL\" → lazy import.\n- rembg u2netp ONNX fixed 320 → own dynamic export; but u2netp collapses above 320 (measured).\n- Guided filter blurred everything (eps too large; thin structures eroded) → rejected. Zoom pass gain < tolerance → rejected.\n- BiRefNet_lite: WASM `std::bad_alloc` even at 512 (fixed-1024 export); WebGPU headless \"Too many storage buffers 11 > 10\" (software adapter limit) → measured quality via PyTorch MPS instead.\n- Latest: **RMBG-2.0 is HF-gated** (\"Access restricted… log in\"); **BiRefNet full failed**: `RuntimeError: Input type (float) and bias type (c10::Half)` — model loads in fp16; needs `model.float()` or `.half()` input.\n\n## 5. Problem Solving\n- Shipped 0.2.0 to production (applied 2 migrations via MCP; user ran the constraint SQL; deploy verified).\n- Discovered and fixed: default branch was `develop`; CI never ran on develop PRs; imgly default download was ~100 MB (not \"a few MB\"); Sentry Session Replay was on; no backups on Supabase free plan.\n- Model bake-off results (IoU vs visually-correct reference, 34 photos): u2netp+sharpen 10 under bar/mean 0.972/worst 0.801; **BiRefNet_lite 7/0.979/0.827 (best; trousers 0.997, chain 0.86; DIS5K-trained, MIT weights)**; SAM2 tiny 25/0.948; small 20/0.949; base+ 13/0.958 (256px decoder limits edges); U²-Net full 8/0.949/worst 0.170 (catastrophic on Angels' Share bottle); ensemble no help. Contact sheets in `scratch/*sheet*.png`.\n\n## 6. All user messages (this span)\n- \"merged, go next\"\n- \"give me decisions one more time, i canceled it\"\n- \"1. A 2.We should think about that, what will be better. 3.A if u are sure. and drop regarless ofc if we should do it\"\n- \"did u make a branch review for last pr?\"\n- \"put .env.example inside, its only example file?\"\n- \"full branch review maden?\"\n- \"we cant fix it right now?\"\n- \"ur recommendation\"\n- \"so now how it works\"\n- \"but it works with all colours same?\"\n- \"and all other things that we made with generator works on all colours or only on trios\"\n- \"if its okay, merge\"\n- \"okay, we will start but later, i will say, so can we push all commits code from develop to main to give users try our new features, but firsty i want to build new function like show a small pop up notification that will shortly say whats new, what fixed\"\n- \"make it further, BUT WHY DEVELOP BRANCH IS A DEFAULT BRANCH, it should be main and developo branch is only pre production brooooo\"\n- \"maybe just make pop up menu about update, then tap on it and it will open list\"\n- \"i will say if its okay\"\n- \"and move it to closet page, not generator\"\n- \"bro, can u do it all, im lost\"\n- \"i make a sql, thats all what we should do?\"\n- \"okay, so whats now, i found that - The bag-echo criterion… [FUTURE items] and also parfums (we should parse them from website…)\"\n- \"okay, but i wanna add some new 1.Add German and russian and ukrainian 2.Revoke quiz… 3.Cookies 4.…tomorrow 5.…link to a cloth… 6.Share look… 7.…button to regenerate 8.Broken page, try another look button… 9. Privacy Policy and Terms. 10.…upload a lot images…\"\n- \"and also connect stripe, its time to make public our work on 1 version\"\n- \"forget to add all another plans that we planned before\"\n- \"we can rebuild that system with background, so we cant be issued\"\n- \"about amber, what is that and which price\"\n- \"explain me amber man, maybe we have free posibility\"\n- \"go with amber, so whats next\"\n- \"did u made a full review of that function, dont merge without my permission\"\n- \"'…fitcheck-privacy-terms-review.md' look at this and about vat, maybe better to use paddle instead of stripe, but for now it doesnt make sense\"\n- \"we would do paddle but a lot later, when we would have enough revenue, so whats next in plan?\"\n- \"go\"\n- \"okay, but u should make me comparison after swap and then after 1 update and 2 update, to understand that it was better… also u forgot to make branch review before commit and push\"\n- \"pr didnt catch that, cause it doenst make e2e, i dont know why\"\n- \"wasnt leaked api keys???\"\n- \"merge conflict\"\n- \"error in e2e test\"\n- \"we can add test assets to dev branch but exclude it from merging to main branch\"\n- \"privacy and terms are only visible in setting, also we need to add in plan creation of backups, also what can we also see or add from sentry.io, also make it sense to add doppler…, and where i can see analytics(appfigures…)… did u done things from …review.md, u didnt checked steps on the end of md file\"\n- \"go\"\n- \"go with 1, then i will say u whats next, dont forget also do updates 1 and 2 for our cutout model\"\n- \"1 is Privacy/Terms visibility… write in roadmap updrade for cutout background model update 1 and 2\"\n- \"we will do for now only manuel backups mate\"\n- \"update please now roadmap, if we done with something\"\n- \"l2 owner checklist?\"\n- \"so are u updated it that we right now can update?\"\n- \"i mean in legal and terms, did u all what we can without lawyer?\"\n- \"how to accept dpa in dashboadrds?\"\n- \"[Supabase image] But do we need it mate, its so stupid to hold it in our website\"\n- \"[Stripe image] help, also dont forget to make in google console production mode\"\n- \"[image] is that all?\"\n- \"send invoices?\"\n- \"[Stripe images: pricing model / recurring payments]\"\n- \"also add button to cancel subscription, we forgot it, and what to make here, we will have month and annual subscription\"\n- \"[image] we are adding products in stripe, so help me to add this subscription in stripe, what to write\"\n- \"its real account now [image]\"\n- \"[statement descriptor image]\"\n- \"maybe switch stripe to ukraine, cause i dont have swiss bank account\"\n- \"[Wise images ×4]\"; \"[image] basic is enough?\"\n- \"check which is better for us, neon yuh or zak\"\n- \"so we need only one\"\n- \"okay, i will do it, go with L1b\"\n- \"work\"\n- \"show me result\"\n- \"bro, its bad, we need better, find better model, and maybe this is good BiRefNet\"\n- \"no, i found something else SAM 2, is ist good\"\n- \"i dont want have questions to lawyer, maybe sam 2.1 has bigger model\"\n- \"wait, so just use with mit license, just test RMBG-2.0, BiRefNet and our old model, that we used, whats better, like take all models that theoreticaly works for us and test and give me comparison on photos, i will see difference\"\n\n## 7. Pending Tasks\n- **Model bake-off (current):** get RMBG-2.0 running (HF gated — needs user's HF login/acceptance or skip with note; non-commercial licence), fix BiRefNet full (fp16 input/`model.float()`), optionally RMBG-1.4; then a **visual contact sheet** across ALL models (imgly ISNet baseline, u2netp shipped, U²-Net full, BiRefNet_lite, BiRefNet full, SAM 2.1 tiny/small/base+, RMBG-2.0) on representative photos + metrics table, for the user to judge.\n- Open PRs awaiting user's go: **#83** (legal links) and **#84** (L1b sharpen). No merging without explicit go.\n- Roadmap (docs/superpowers/plans/roadmap-2026-09-14.md): L3-pre Google OAuth production mode; L3 Stripe (checkout withdrawal checkbox, cancel button, monthly+annual EUR — annual price undecided, €50/yr suggested); L4 account deletion; O1 manual backups (optional `scripts/backup.mjs`); O3 Sentry alerts/release/uptime; O4 Doppler; O5 enable Vercel Analytics; D batch upload; E share look; P1–P3; owner checklist (DPAs, lawyer for Terms/subscription, SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN on Vercel).\n- User is opening a Yuh Pro bank account for Stripe payouts; Stripe onboarding in progress.\n\n## 8. Current Work\nRunning the comprehensive model comparison the user asked for. Just executed `scratch/export/hf_seg.py` (generic `AutoModelForImageSegmentation` runner, args: repo, out dir, size) for `briaai/RMBG-2.0` → failed: *\"Access to model briaai/RMBG-2.0 is restricted. You must have access to it and be authenticated\"*; and `ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet` (full) → failed: *\"RuntimeError: Input type (float) and bias type (c10::Half) should be the same\"* (model weights fp16; need `.float()` on model or `.half()` input). Zero cutouts produced for both. Existing candidate outputs and parity JSONs: u2netp stage0/stage1, birefnet_lite, sam2_tiny/small/baseplus, u2net_full, u2_ensemble; baselines (imgly ISNet) in `scratch/baseline/`. Sheet generator: `scratch/result-sheet.mjs` (edit `pick`, sources, output filename).\n\n## 9. Optional Next Step\nContinue the bake-off exactly as requested: *\"take all models that theoreticaly works for us and test and give me comparison on photos, i will see difference.\"* Concretely: (1) fix BiRefNet full by loading with `torch_dtype=torch.float32` / `model.float()` in `hf_seg.py` and run at 1024; (2) for RMBG-2.0, tell the user it's HF-gated (needs `huggingface-cli login` + accepting Bria's terms on the model page) and non-commercial, and either get a token from them or mark it \"not testable\"; optionally try RMBG-1.4 (also gated); (3) score each with `FROM_DIR=scratch/candidates/<dir> node scripts/cutout-harness/run.mjs`; (4) build a multi-column contact sheet (imgly · u2netp · U²-Net full · BiRefNet_lite · BiRefNet full · SAM2 base+ · RMBG-2.0 if available) on ~8 representative photos (chain, trousers, both sneakers, white shirt, Angels' Share, Kilian, knit polo) plus the summary table (under-bar / mean / worst / licence / size), and present it for the user's own judgement — without merging or changing the shipped default until they decide.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/1curafu/.claude/projects/-Users-1curafu-Desktop-Fitcheck-Fitcheck/8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"78814d49-8733-4189-92f3-af01a8e34132","timestamp":"2026-09-16T10:14:41.735Z","session_id":"b948f157-4213-4e56-bd64-c9eb07cc152a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-refinement","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
