{"parentUuid":"f38644e7-7fcb-4d40-95fa-30df34288240","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14999487 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4da3e9f0-0af2-43b6-8863-40c113eeb7cb","timestamp":"2026-09-16T16:04:59.133Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14999487 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-refinement","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
{"parentUuid":"4da3e9f0-0af2-43b6-8863-40c113eeb7cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf7QLS9h7WmabXuV2bc8P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Half right. AGPL doesn't ban commercial use — it bans *closed-source* commercial use. The deal is: if you serve `@imgly` to users, your whole app must be available under AGPL too.\n\nYour repo is already public under **GPL-3.0**, so you're most of the way there. What it would actually mean:\n\n1. **Relicense Fitcheck GPL-3 → AGPL-3** (GPL-3 alone is not enough; GPL doesn't cover network use, AGPL does, and imgly's AGPL requires your combined work to be AGPL). One file change, permitted since you're the sole author.\n2. **Anyone can clone and self-host Fitcheck, including paying users.** You'd sell the hosted service, not the code. Some businesses do fine with that (Plausible, Cal.com); for a consumer app with no infra moat it's a real risk — a competitor can take the generator, the rules, everything.\n3. **The dataset problem doesn't go away.** imgly's default model is trained on DIS5K, whose terms are non-commercial. That's a separate, weaker claim (dataset terms binding a downstream model is legally murky), but it's exactly the kind of thing you said you don't want lawyer questions about.\n4. imgly sells a commercial licence for exactly this case — that's the clean route if you want their model closed-source. Price is \"contact sales\".\n\nSo: theoretically yes, if you're happy being fully AGPL and losing the code moat. Practically, BiRefNet lite (MIT, 0.979 vs imgly's edge only on one sneaker) gets you 95 % of the way with no strings. Your call — if you pick AGPL I'll swap back and relicense; if not, I build the WebGPU BiRefNet path."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":526,"cache_read_input_tokens":117979,"output_tokens":573,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":526,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":117979,"cache_creation_input_tokens":526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":526},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf7QLPxE4jmjD6fsCCcLg","type":"assistant","uuid":"60eaffe0-14f5-41f3-b1d5-c989ddfdd534","timestamp":"2026-09-16T16:05:10.022Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-refinement","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
