{"parentUuid":"64012585-2fc9-47e0-911d-a9e715503abe","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4236be89-a222-44d3-864f-75c76b867d88","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kj5d4RYhsshwX5K6dc8ikL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"best open source background removal model 2026 MIT Apache license commercial use\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Best Open Source Windows Background Removers 2026\",\"url\":\"https://sourceforge.net/directory/background-removers/\"},{\"title\":\"Best background removal tools in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://claid.ai/blog/article/best-background-removal-apps\"},{\"title\":\"AI Background Removal Models: SAM 3.1, Bria, BEN v2, BiRefNet Compared (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://invideo.io/blog/ai-background-removal-models/\"},{\"title\":\"Open Background Removal Models | withoutBG\",\"url\":\"https://withoutbg.com/models\"},{\"title\":\"Top Open-Source AI Video Background Generators for Developers in 2026 — AI Daily Shot\",\"url\":\"https://aidailyshot.com/blog/top-open-source-ai-video-background-generators-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Best AI Background Removers in 2026: Free vs Paid — AI Free Forever\",\"url\":\"https://aifreeforever.com/blog/best-ai-background-removers\"},{\"title\":\"2026 Best Software Awards are here!See the list\",\"url\":\"https://www.g2.com/sellers/background-remover-ai\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the best open-source background removal models for 2026 with permissive licenses suitable for commercial use:\n\n## MIT License Models (Unrestricted Commercial Use)\n\n**BiRefNet** - BiRefNet ships under the MIT license, which means unrestricted commercial use. BiRefNet (bilateral-reference segmentation, MIT) is the open workhorse behind several commercial products, including Bria's, with variants for general use, portraits, matting, and 2048² high-res work, running ~17 FPS. BiRefNet processes a 1024×1024 image at 17 FPS in FP16 mode, using roughly 3.5 GB of VRAM.\n\n## Apache 2.0 License Models\n\n**withoutBG Open Model** - Apache-2.0 open-weights background removal model from withoutBG. Self-host via Python, Docker, or Mac.\n\n**rembg** - rembg is the most widely deployed open-source background removal tool, functioning as a Python library, CLI tool, HTTP server, and Docker container. The latest release (June 2026) supports Python 3.11 through 3.14 and runs on ONNX Runtime, which means it works on CPU, NVIDIA GPU (CUDA), and AMD GPU (ROCm).\n\nAll of the tools in this review are 100% open-source and free to use under permissive licenses (MIT, Apache 2.0, or GPLv3). For commercial use, BiRefNet's MIT license provides the most unrestricted legal framework, while both withoutBG's Apache 2.0 model and rembg also support commercial applications.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7751b754-4f53-4ac2-8416-e27e1afcb7aa","timestamp":"2026-09-16T16:07:03.990Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"best open source background removal model 2026 MIT Apache license commercial use","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01YGh8PpRP518RoP3d8JfKyB","content":[{"title":"Best Open Source Windows Background Removers 2026","url":"https://sourceforge.net/directory/background-removers/"},{"title":"Best background removal tools in 2026","url":"https://claid.ai/blog/article/best-background-removal-apps"},{"title":"AI Background Removal Models: SAM 3.1, Bria, BEN v2, BiRefNet Compared (2026)","url":"https://invideo.io/blog/ai-background-removal-models/"},{"title":"Open Background Removal Models | withoutBG","url":"https://withoutbg.com/models"},{"title":"Top Open-Source AI Video Background Generators for Developers in 2026 — AI Daily Shot","url":"https://aidailyshot.com/blog/top-open-source-ai-video-background-generators-2026"},{"title":"Best AI Background Removers in 2026: Free vs Paid — AI Free Forever","url":"https://aifreeforever.com/blog/best-ai-background-removers"},{"title":"2026 Best Software Awards are here!See the list","url":"https://www.g2.com/sellers/background-remover-ai"}]},"Based on the search results, here are the best open-source background removal models for 2026 with permissive licenses suitable for commercial use:\n\n## MIT License Models (Unrestricted Commercial Use)\n\n**BiRefNet** - BiRefNet ships under the MIT license, which means unrestricted commercial use. BiRefNet (bilateral-reference segmentation, MIT) is the open workhorse behind several commercial products, including Bria's, with variants for general use, portraits, matting, and 2048² high-res work, running ~17 FPS. BiRefNet processes a 1024×1024 image at 17 FPS in FP16 mode, using roughly 3.5 GB of VRAM.\n\n## Apache 2.0 License Models\n\n**withoutBG Open Model** - Apache-2.0 open-weights background removal model from withoutBG. Self-host via Python, Docker, or Mac.\n\n**rembg** - rembg is the most widely deployed open-source background removal tool, functioning as a Python library, CLI tool, HTTP server, and Docker container. The latest release (June 2026) supports Python 3.11 through 3.14 and runs on ONNX Runtime, which means it works on CPU, NVIDIA GPU (CUDA), and AMD GPU (ROCm).\n\nAll of the tools in this review are 100% open-source and free to use under permissive licenses (MIT, Apache 2.0, or GPLv3). For commercial use, BiRefNet's MIT license provides the most unrestricted legal framework, while both withoutBG's Apache 2.0 model and rembg also support commercial applications."],"durationSeconds":7.161061542000621,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"64012585-2fc9-47e0-911d-a9e715503abe","session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-refinement","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
