{"parentUuid":"3ce311ac-8122-4b5c-8dab-001d600d0588","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf7TZVDChie4s4nXz8vWj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Short version: I can't give you a per-image time for BiRefNet lite in the browser yet, because it doesn't run in the browser yet.\n\nWhat I know:\n- **On this Mac via PyTorch (GPU): ~0.5–0.9 s per image.** That's not what a phone would see.\n- **In the browser** it's been failing, and I've been fixing it step by step:\n  1. WebGPU crashed with \"too many storage buffers\" — BiRefNet's graph has Split/Concat nodes with 1024 inputs. I rewrote the ONNX to split them into small trees. **That crash is gone.**\n  2. Now it fails with `std::bad_alloc` — the WASM side runs out of memory even on WebGPU (parts of the model fall back to CPU). I was checking memory settings when you interrupted.\n\nSo the honest state: quality is measured and good; **browser feasibility is not proven.** The remaining risk is real — a 115 MB model at 1024 px may simply not fit in a mobile browser's memory, which is exactly why u2netp was chosen.\n\nTwo ways forward:\n- **A. Keep pushing the browser path** (memory settings, 768 px input, fp16 activations). Maybe another hour; may still fail on phones.\n- **B. Run BiRefNet lite on a server** (Modal/Replicate GPU, ~$0.001–0.005 per image). Guaranteed to work, ~1–2 s per image, but it breaks the \"zero per-image cost\" rule and the photo leaves the device.\n\nWhich one?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":533,"cache_read_input_tokens":170909,"output_tokens":505,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":533,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_token