{"parentUuid":"4a4499e3-9bf5-4a46-9391-8b3ac1fb7f15","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0e509fe1-2cde-47e5-88ff-217435c2c5f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ASaXfrNuJzriG5Aa46ZycN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Vercel functions fluid compute memory limit hobby pro 2026 max duration bundle size 250MB\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Vercel Functions Limits\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/limitations\"},{\"title\":\"Limits\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/docs/limits\"},{\"title\":\"Configuring Memory and CPU for Vercel Functions\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/configuring-functions/memory\"},{\"title\":\"Legacy Usage & Pricing for Functions\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/usage-and-pricing/legacy-pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Vercel Free Tier: Hobby Plan Limits (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://costbench.com/software/developer-tools/vercel/free-plan/\"},{\"title\":\"Vercel Pricing 2026: Plans, Limits & Costs | Temps\",\"url\":\"https://temps.sh/blog/vercel-pricing-complete-guide-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Vercel free tier limits in 2026: what you actually get on Hobby\",\"url\":\"https://www.promptstoproduct.com/vercel-free-tier-limits\"},{\"title\":\"Vercel Hobby Plan\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/docs/plans/hobby\"}]\n\nNow let me search for more specific information about bundle size and fluid compute limits:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Python Vercel Functions bundle size limit increased to 500MB - Vercel\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/changelog/python-vercel-functions-bundle-size-limit-increased-to-500mb\"},{\"title\":\"Troubleshooting Build Error: \\\"Serverless Function has exceeded the unzipped maximum size of 250 MB\\\" | Vercel Knowledge Base\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/kb/guide/troubleshooting-function-250mb-limit\"},{\"title\":\"Bun runtime now supports large functions and extended max duration - Vercel\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/changelog/bun-runtime-now-supports-large-functions-and-extended-max-duration\"},{\"title\":\"Vercel Functions Limits\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/limitations\"},{\"title\":\"Configuring Maximum Duration for Vercel Functions\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/configuring-functions/duration\"},{\"title\":\"Python - Serverless Function has exceeded the unzipped maximum size - Help - Vercel Community\",\"url\":\"https://community.vercel.com/t/python-serverless-function-has-exceeded-the-unzipped-maximum-size/7395\"},{\"title\":\"Vercel FFmpeg Video Processing: Serverless Function Limits in 2026 | Very Good FFmpeg\",\"url\":\"https://verygoodffmpeg.com/blog/vercel-ffmpeg-video-processing-serverless-functions-limits-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Limits\",\"url\":\"https://vercel.com/docs/limits\"},{\"title\":\"Vercel Function Size Limit: Fix or Migrate to Containers\",\"url\":\"https://opsily.com/blog/vercel-serverless-function-size-limit-exceeded\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's a comprehensive summary of Vercel Functions limits for Hobby and Pro plans with Fluid Compute in 2026:\n\n## Memory Limits\n\nHobby users will always use the default memory size of 2 GB (1 vCPU). With fluid compute enabled on Pro and Enterprise plans, the default memory size is 2 GB (1 vCPU) and can be upgraded to 4 GB / 2 vCPUs.\n\n## Bundle Size\n\nThe standard maximum uncompressed size is 250 MB. However, large functions raise the standard 250MB package size limit to 5GB, and extended max duration raises the generally available 800-second ceiling to 1800 seconds for Pro and Enterprise teams. Both features require Fluid compute to be enabled.\n\n## Maximum Duration\n\nThe 800 second maximum is generally available for Pro and Enterprise teams with fluid compute. The 1800 second extended maximum is in beta.\n\n## Python Functions\n\nNote that the bundle size limit for Python Vercel Functions has increased from 250MB to 500MB, giving Python more flexibility than Node.js/Bun functions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cc567fe4-87ec-4f4c-af58-dc222cf089ef","timestamp":"2026-09-16T17:17:04.088Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Vercel functions fluid compute memory limit hobby pro 2026 max duration bundle size 250MB","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013tm29hkpzoAwHdz8hU5QYF","content":[{"title":"Vercel Functions Limits","url":"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/limitations"},{"title":"Limits","url":"https://vercel.com/docs/limits"},{"title":"Configuring Memory and CPU for Vercel Functions","url":"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/configuring-functions/memory"},{"title":"Legacy Usage & Pricing for Functions","url":"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/usage-and-pricing/legacy-pricing"},{"title":"Vercel Free Tier: Hobby Plan Limits (2026)","url":"https://costbench.com/software/developer-tools/vercel/free-plan/"},{"title":"Vercel Pricing 2026: Plans, Limits & Costs | Temps","url":"https://temps.sh/blog/vercel-pricing-complete-guide-2026"},{"title":"Vercel free tier limits in 2026: what you actually get on Hobby","url":"https://www.promptstoproduct.com/vercel-free-tier-limits"},{"title":"Vercel Hobby Plan","url":"https://vercel.com/docs/plans/hobby"}]},"Now let me search for more specific information about bundle size and fluid compute limits:",{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018AZuJaWq3Av2zfZhAhN9mD","content":[{"title":"Python Vercel Functions bundle size limit increased to 500MB - Vercel","url":"https://vercel.com/changelog/python-vercel-functions-bundle-size-limit-increased-to-500mb"},{"title":"Troubleshooting Build Error: \"Serverless Function has exceeded the unzipped maximum size of 250 MB\" | Vercel Knowledge Base","url":"https://vercel.com/kb/guide/troubleshooting-function-250mb-limit"},{"title":"Bun runtime now supports large functions and extended max duration - Vercel","url":"https://vercel.com/changelog/bun-runtime-now-supports-large-functions-and-extended-max-duration"},{"title":"Vercel Functions Limits","url":"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/limitations"},{"title":"Configuring Maximum Duration for Vercel Functions","url":"https://vercel.com/docs/functions/configuring-functions/duration"},{"title":"Python - Serverless Function has exceeded the unzipped maximum size - Help - Vercel Community","url":"https://community.vercel.com/t/python-serverless-function-has-exceeded-the-unzipped-maximum-size/7395"},{"title":"Vercel FFmpeg Video Processing: Serverless Function Limits in 2026 | Very Good FFmpeg","url":"https://verygoodffmpeg.com/blog/vercel-ffmpeg-video-processing-serverless-functions-limits-2026"},{"title":"Limits","url":"https://vercel.com/docs/limits"},{"title":"Vercel Function Size Limit: Fix or Migrate to Containers","url":"https://opsily.com/blog/vercel-serverless-function-size-limit-exceeded"}]},"Based on the search results, here's a comprehensive summary of Vercel Functions limits for Hobby and Pro plans with Fluid Compute in 2026:\n\n## Memory Limits\n\nHobby users will always use the default memory size of 2 GB (1 vCPU). With fluid compute enabled on Pro and Enterprise plans, the default memory size is 2 GB (1 vCPU) and can be upgraded to 4 GB / 2 vCPUs.\n\n## Bundle Size\n\nThe standard maximum uncompressed size is 250 MB. However, large functions raise the standard 250MB package size limit to 5GB, and extended max duration raises the generally available 800-second ceiling to 1800 seconds for Pro and Enterprise teams. Both features require Fluid compute to be enabled.\n\n## Maximum Duration\n\nThe 800 second maximum is generally available for Pro and Enterprise teams with fluid compute. The 1800 second extended maximum is in beta.\n\n## Python Functions\n\nNote that the bundle size limit for Python Vercel Functions has increased from 250MB to 500MB, giving Python more flexibility than Node.js/Bun functions."],"durationSeconds":8.271139459000901,"searchCount":2},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4a4499e3-9bf5-4a46-9391-8b3ac1fb7f15","session_id":