{"parentUuid":"1642144c-d1fc-4c6d-a1c6-62eddee89237","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf7X4uEV1hktWFqQXBuFc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Real photo (48 MP, black trousers on a textured white blanket — a hard case: dark on bright, busy background):\n\n- **At phone size all four look fine** — IoU 0.989 for u2netp vs imgly. This is the honest headline: on a whole-garment photo the difference is invisible.\n- **Zoomed in**, u2netp's edge is soft and wavy: the hem crop shows a blurred, slightly eaten edge with a faint grey halo, the waistband crop shows fuzz on the left edge. That's the 320 px mask upscaled 25×.\n- **BiRefNet lite and full are crisp and identical** here — clean edge at the hem, no halo. Lite = full on this photo.\n- **imgly** is between: cleaner than u2netp, softer than BiRefNet.\n\nSo for real phone photos: u2netp is *acceptable*, BiRefNet is *clean*, and you only see it if you zoom. In the app the cutout is displayed at ~400 px wide — where they look the same. Whether the edge quality is worth $0.001/image on fal is your call; the cutout also goes to Haiku for tagging, which doesn't care about edges."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_read_input_tokens":268726,"output_tokens":385,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":469,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":385,"cache_read_input_tokens":268726,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":469},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf7X4pJKBuP5vutaC