{"parentUuid":"097fd029-e645-4743-bbcd-1b5d6d2814e3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf7rQe7R6Au2BSsU3N3Kk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm using the writing-plans skill to create the implementation plan."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":311787,"output_tokens":11401,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":573,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11401,"cache_read_input_tokens":311787,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":573},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf7rQapikY85BZKcxGyhM","attributionSkill":"superpowers:writing-plans","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"aff984ea-931d-4bbf-9e1f-87f3bf2105c3","timestamp":"2026-09-16T21:46:55.353Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-refinement","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
{"parentUuid":"aff984ea-931d-4bbf-9e1f-87f3bf2105c3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf7rQe7R6Au2BSsU3N3Kk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BkH4YerR33rp2t51as32Nm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck/docs/superpowers/plans/todo/2026-09-16-cutout-rotation.md","content":"# Cutout Rotation Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** A garment photographed sideways or upside down ends up stored upright — Haiku drafts the rotation, the confirm screen shows it applied, and one button lets the user correct it before saving.\n\n**Architecture:** Rotation is NOT a tag and NOT a DB column: it is baked into the stored cutout and thumbnail at confirm time, so every reader (closet grid, flat-lay, Haiku re-tagging, share cards) sees an upright item with no per-view work. The model returns `rotation` (degrees clockwise: 0/90/180/270) alongside the tags because \"which way is up\" is semantic (a belt lying flat IS upright; trousers lying flat are not) — a geometric rule cannot decide it. The client keeps the uploaded cutout as the base, previews `rotate(base, rotation)`, and on save re-encodes and upserts the rotated cutout + thumb over the same storage paths. The original photo is never rotated (it is the photo).\n\n**Tech Stack:** Zod 4 + Anthropic structured outputs (`lib/ai/tagging-schema.ts`), canvas rotation on the client (`lib/images/`), Supabase Storage upsert in the existing Server Actions, Playwright WebKit e2e.\n\n**Spec:** This document (decided in conversation 2026-09-16; EXIF orientation was verified to already work end-to-end — `e2e/capture-exif.spec.ts`).\n\n## Global Constraints\n\n- Branch `feat/cutout-rotation` from `develop`; PR into `develop`. Never merge without an explicit go.\n- Full branch mutation review before push (memory: full-branch-review-before-pr).\n- Few code comments: one note per surprising decision.\n- `Test assets/` is never committed; e2e fixtures are the drawn `e2e/fixtures/garment*.jpg`.\n- `npm run test:run`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build` green; e2e for capture specs green (`set -a; source .env.local; set +a; npx playwright test e2e/capture*.spec.ts`).\n- Structured-output schemas go through `forStructuredOutput()`; no validation keywords.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Model returns `rotation`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `lib/ai/tagging-schema.ts` (after `export type Tags`, and `taggingJsonSchema`)\n- Modify: `lib/ai/parse-tags.ts:7-20`\n- Modify: `lib/ai/tag-item.ts:26-57`\n- Modify: `lib/ai/tagging-prompt.ts` (append a `rotation` paragraph)\n- Test: `lib/ai/__tests__/tagging-schema.test.ts`, `lib/ai/__tests__/parse-tags.test.ts`, `lib/ai/__tests__/tag-item-prompt.test.ts`\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Produces: `export const ROTATIONS = [0, 90, 180, 270] as const; export type Rotation = 0 | 90 | 180 | 270; export const RotationSchema`; `export function parseTaggingResponse(text: string): { tags: Tags; rotation: Rotation }`; `tagItem()` now resolves to `{ tags: Tags; rotation: Rotation }`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests**\n\nAppend to `lib/ai/__tests__/tagging-schema.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { RotationSchema, ROTATIONS, taggingJsonSchema } from \"../tagging-schema\";\n\ntest(\"rotation is one of four clockwise quarter turns\", () => {\n  for (const r of ROTATIONS) expect(RotationSchema.parse(r)).toBe(r);\n  expect(() => RotationSchema.parse(45)).toThrow();\n  expect(() => RotationSchema.parse(\"90\")).toThrow();\n});\n\ntest(\"the model is asked for rotation, as an enum of numbers\", () => {\n  const props = (taggingJsonSchema as { properties: Record<string, unknown> }).properties;\n  expect(props.rotation).toEqual({ type: \"number\", enum: [0, 90, 180, 270] });\n  expect((taggingJsonSchema as { required: string[] }).required).toContain(\"rotation\");\n});\n```\n\nAppend to `lib/ai/__tests__/parse-tags.test.ts` (reuse the file's existing valid-tags JSON fixture — call it `valid` below; if the file names it differently, use that name):\n\n```ts\nimport { parseTaggingResponse } from \"../parse-tags\";\n\ntest(\"parseTaggingResponse splits rotation from the tags\", () => {\n  const { tags, rotation } = parseTaggingResponse(JSON.stringify({ ...valid, rotation: 90 }));\n  expect(rotation).toBe(90);\n  expect(\"rotation\" in tags).toBe(false);\n});\n\ntest(\"a response without rotation is upright\", () => {\n  expect(parseTaggingResponse(JSON.stringify(valid)).rotation).toBe(0);\n});\n```\n\nAppend to `lib/ai/__tests__/tag-item-prompt.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\ntest(\"the prompt defines rotation as clockwise quarter turns and names the flat-lay exceptions\", () => {\n  expect(PROMPT).toContain(\"rotation\");\n  expect(PROMPT).toContain(\"clockwise\");\n  for (const r of [\"0\", \"90\", \"180\", \"270\"]) expect(PROMPT).toContain(r);\n  expect(PROMPT.toLowerCase()).toContain(\"belt\");\n});\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run them to see them fail**\n\nRun: `npx vitest run lib/ai`\nExpected: FAIL — `RotationSchema`/`parseTaggingResponse` not exported; prompt lacks \"rotation\".\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Schema**\n\nIn `lib/ai/tagging-schema.ts`, after `export type Tags = z.infer<typeof TagSchema>;`:\n\n```ts\n/**\n * Degrees CLOCKWISE to turn the photo so the item is upright as worn. Not a\n * tag: it is applied to the stored cutout at confirm time and never persisted.\n */\nexport const ROTATIONS = [0, 90, 180, 270] as const;\nexport type Rotation = (typeof ROTATIONS)[number];\nexport const RotationSchema = z.union([z.literal(0), z.literal(90), z.literal(180), z.literal(270)]);\n\n/** What the model answers: every tag a photo can settle, plus which way is up. */\nexport const TaggingResponseSchema = TagSchema.omit({ fit_source: true }).extend({\n  rotation: RotationSchema,\n});\n```\n\nReplace the `taggingJsonSchema` definition with:\n\n```ts\nexport const taggingJsonSchema = forStructuredOutput(\n  z.toJSONSchema(TaggingResponseSchema),\n) as Record<string, unknown>;\n```\n\nCheck what Zod 4 emits for the literal union: run `node -e 'const {z}=require(\"zod\");console.log(JSON.stringify(z.toJSONSchema(z.union([z.literal(0),z.literal(90),z.literal(180),z.literal(270)]))))'`. If it emits `anyOf` of `const`s instead of `{type:\"number\",enum:[...]}`, replace `RotationSchema` with `z.literal([0, 90, 180, 270])` (Zod 4 multi-value literal) and re-check — the test pins the enum shape because Anthropic's structured outputs accept `enum`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Parser**\n\nIn `lib/ai/parse-tags.ts`, keep `parseTagText` (tests and fixtures use it) and add:\n\n```ts\nimport { RotationSchema, TagSchema, WEARABLE_CATEGORIES, type Rotation, type Tags } from \"./tagging-schema\";\n\nexport function parseTaggingResponse(text: string): { tags: Tags; rotation: Rotation } {\n  let json: unknown;\n  try {\n    json = JSON.parse(text);\n  } catch {\n    throw new Error(\"Tagging response was not JSON\");\n  }\n  const { rotation, ...rest } = json as Record<string, unknown>;\n  return {\n    tags: TagSchema.parse({ fit_source: null, ...rest }),\n    rotation: rotation === undefined ? 0 : RotationSchema.parse(rotation),\n  };\n}\n```\n\nand make `parseTagText` delegate: `export function parseTagText(text: string): Tags { return parseTaggingResponse(text).tags; }`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: tagItem and the stub**\n\nIn `lib/ai/tag-item.ts`: import `parseTaggingResponse` instead of `parseTagText`; `stubbedTags()` returns `parseTaggingResponse(JSON.stringify({ ...same fields..., rotation: 0 }))`; `tagItem` returns `parseTaggingResponse(text)`. Update the trailing comment to \"validated draft tags + rotation\".\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Prompt**\n\nAppend to `PROMPT` in `lib/ai/tagging-prompt.ts`, before the closing backtick:\n\n```\nrotation — degrees CLOCKWISE to turn the photo so the item is upright as it is worn or \\\ncarried: 0, 90, 180 or 270. Upright means collar, waistband, hood or bag opening at the top and \\\nshoes standing on their soles. Items that are laid flat lengthways — a belt, a chain, a tie, a \\\nscarf, a watch strap — are upright at 0 when they run left to right. Answer 0 when unsure.\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the tests**\n\nRun: `npx vitest run lib/ai && npx tsc --noEmit`\nExpected: PASS; tsc reports `app/closet/upload/actions.ts` because `tagItem` now returns an object (fixed in Task 3) — that is the only error.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add lib/ai\ngit commit -m \"Tagging: the model answers which way is up\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Rotate a cutout on the client\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `lib/images/rotate.ts`\n- Test: `lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts`\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Produces: `rotatedSize(w, h, rotation): { width, height }`, `rotateRGBA(data: Uint8ClampedArray, width, height, rotation): { data: Uint8ClampedArray; width; height }` (pure), `rotateBlob(source: Blob, rotation: Rotation): Promise<Blob>` (browser; returns a PNG, alpha preserved; `rotation === 0` returns `source` untouched).\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests**\n\n`lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { rotateRGBA, rotatedSize } from \"../rotate\";\n\n// 2×1 image: red pixel left, blue pixel right.\nconst px = (r: number, g: number, b: number, a = 255) => [r, g, b, a];\nconst src = new Uint8ClampedArray([...px(255, 0, 0), ...px(0, 0, 255)]);\n\ntest(\"0 is identity\", () => {\n  const out = rotateRGBA(src, 2, 1, 0);\n  expect([out.width, out.height]).toEqual([2, 1]);\n  expect(Array.from(out.data)).toEqual(Array.from(src));\n});\n\ntest(\"90 clockwise puts the left pixel on top\", () => {\n  const out = rotateRGBA(src, 2, 1, 90);\n  expect([out.width, out.height]).toEqual([1, 2]);\n  expect(Array.from(out.data)).toEqual([...px(255, 0, 0), ...px(0, 0, 255)]);\n});\n\ntest(\"180 mirrors both axes\", () => {\n  const out = rotateRGBA(src, 2, 1, 180);\n  expect([out.width, out.height]).toEqual([2, 1]);\n  expect(Array.from(out.data)).toEqual([...px(0, 0, 255), ...px(255, 0, 0)]);\n});\n\ntest(\"270 clockwise puts the right pixel on top\", () => {\n  const out = rotateRGBA(src, 2, 1, 270);\n  expect([out.width, out.height]).toEqual([1, 2]);\n  expect(Array.from(out.data)).toEqual([...px(0, 0, 255), ...px(255, 0, 0)]);\n});\n\ntest(\"alpha survives\", () => {\n  const t = new Uint8ClampedArray([...px(1, 2, 3, 0), ...px(4, 5, 6, 128)]);\n  expect(Array.from(rotateRGBA(t, 2, 1, 90).data)).toEqual([...px(1, 2, 3, 0), ...px(4, 5, 6, 128)]);\n});\n\ntest(\"rotatedSize swaps on quarter turns only\", () => {\n  expect(rotatedSize(640, 800, 90)).toEqual({ width: 800, height: 640 });\n  expect(rotatedSize(640, 800, 180)).toEqual({ width: 640, height: 800 });\n});\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run to see them fail**\n\nRun: `npx vitest run lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL — module not found.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement**\n\n`lib/images/rotate.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { Rotation } from \"@/lib/ai/tagging-schema\";\n\nexport function rotatedSize(width: number, height: number, rotation: Rotation) {\n  return rotation % 180 === 0 ? { width, height } : { width: height, height: width };\n}\n\n/** Quarter-turn rotation of RGBA pixels, clockwise. Exact: no resampling. */\nexport function rotateRGBA(data: Uint8ClampedArray, width: number, height: number, rotation: Rotation) {\n  if (rotation === 0) return { data, width, height };\n  const { width: w2, height: h2 } = rotatedSize(width, height, rotation);\n  const out = new Uint8ClampedArray(data.length);\n  for (let y = 0; y < height; y++) {\n    for (let x = 0; x < width; x++) {\n      let nx: number, ny: number;\n      if (rotation === 90) { nx = height - 1 - y; ny = x; }\n      else if (rotation === 180) { nx = width - 1 - x; ny = height - 1 - y; }\n      else { nx = y; ny = width - 1 - x; }\n      const s = (y * width + x) * 4, d = (ny * w2 + nx) * 4;\n      out[d] = data[s]; out[d + 1] = data[s + 1]; out[d + 2] = data[s + 2]; out[d + 3] = data[s + 3];\n    }\n  }\n  return { data: out, width: w2, height: h2 };\n}\n\n/** Browser-only. Returns a PNG so alpha and pixels are untouched; encode afterwards. */\nexport async function rotateBlob(source: Blob, rotation: Rotation): Promise<Blob> {\n  if (rotation === 0) return source;\n  const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(source);\n  const canvas = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n  canvas.width = bitmap.width;\n  canvas.height = bitmap.height;\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n  if (!ctx) throw new Error(\"Canvas unavailable\");\n  ctx.drawImage(bitmap, 0, 0);\n  bitmap.close?.();\n  const src = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  const r = rotateRGBA(src.data, src.width, src.height, rotation);\n  canvas.width = r.width;\n  canvas.height = r.height;\n  ctx.putImageData(new ImageData(r.data, r.width, r.height), 0, 0);\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) =>\n    canvas.toBlob((b) => (b ? resolve(b) : reject(new Error(\"Rotate failed\"))), \"image/png\"),\n  );\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run the tests**\n\nRun: `npx vitest run lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts`\nExpected: PASS (6 tests).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add lib/images/rotate.ts lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"Images: exact quarter-turn rotation of a cutout\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Server Actions carry rotation and accept the rotated blobs\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `app/closet/upload/actions.ts:68-75` (uploadAndTag return) and `:78-107` (confirmItem)\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: `tagItem() → { tags, rotation }` (Task 1); `cutoutFilename`, `thumbFilename` (existing).\n- Produces: `uploadAndTag` returns `{ itemId, imagePath, cutoutPath, thumbPath, tags, rotation }`; `confirmItem(input)` gains optional `rotated?: { cutoutB64: string; mediaType: CutoutMediaType; thumbB64: string | null; thumbMediaType: ThumbMediaType | null }` and returns nothing. When `rotated` is present the cutout and thumb at the draft's paths are REPLACED (upsert, same folder; filenames follow the media type actually produced), and the row is inserted with the resulting paths.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: uploadAndTag**\n\nReplace the tail of `uploadAndTag`:\n\n```ts\n  const { tags, rotation } = await tagItem(form.cutoutB64, form.mediaType);\n  return {\n    itemId,\n    imagePath: `${base}/original.jpg`,\n    cutoutPath: `${base}/${cutoutName}`,\n    thumbPath,\n    tags,\n    rotation,\n  };\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: confirmItem**\n\nReplace `confirmItem` with:\n\n```ts\n// Re-validate the (possibly user-edited) tags and insert the item. When the user\n// rotated the cutout, the rotated blobs replace the uploaded ones first, so the\n// row only ever points at upright images.\nexport async function confirmItem(input: {\n  imagePath: string;\n  cutoutPath: string;\n  thumbPath?: string | null;\n  name?: string | null;\n  brand?: string | null;\n  tags: unknown;\n  rotated?: {\n    cutoutB64: string;\n    mediaType: CutoutMediaType;\n    thumbB64: string | null;\n    thumbMediaType: ThumbMediaType | null;\n  } | null;\n}) {\n  const supabase = await createClient();\n  const {\n    data: { user },\n  } = await supabase.auth.getUser();\n  if (!user) throw new Error(\"Not authenticated\");\n\n  let cutoutPath = input.cutoutPath;\n  let thumbPath = input.thumbPath ?? null;\n  if (input.rotated) {\n    // Same defence as discardDraft: client-supplied paths, checked against the caller.\n    if (!cutoutPath.startsWith(`${user.id}/`)) throw new Error(\"Not your upload\");\n    const base = cutoutPath.slice(0, cutoutPath.lastIndexOf(\"/\"));\n    const nextCutout = `${base}/${cutoutFilename(input.rotated.mediaType)}`;\n    const { error } = await supabase.storage\n      .from(\"wardrobe\")\n      .upload(nextCutout, Buffer.from(input.rotated.cutoutB64, \"base64\"), {\n        contentType: input.rotated.mediaType,\n        upsert: true,\n      });\n    if (error) throw error;\n    const stale = [cutoutPath !== nextCutout ? cutoutPath : null];\n    cutoutPath = nextCutout;\n\n    let nextThumb: string | null = null;\n    if (input.rotated.thumbB64 && input.rotated.thumbMediaType) {\n      nextThumb = `${base}/${thumbFilename(input.rotated.thumbMediaType)}`;\n      const { error: thumbError } = await supabase.storage\n        .from(\"wardrobe\")\n        .upload(nextThumb, Buffer.from(input.rotated.thumbB64, \"base64\"), {\n          contentType: input.rotated.thumbMediaType,\n          upsert: true,\n        });\n      if (thumbError) nextThumb = null;\n    }\n    if (thumbPath && thumbPath !== nextThumb) stale.push(thumbPath);\n    thumbPath = nextThumb;\n    const remove = stale.filter((p): p is string => !!p);\n    if (remove.length) await supabase.storage.from(\"wardrobe\").remove(remove);\n  }\n\n  const tags = TagSchema.parse(input.tags);\n  const row = {\n    ...tagsToItemRow({\n      userId: user.id,\n      imageUrl: input.imagePath,\n      cutoutUrl: cutoutPath,\n      thumbUrl: thumbPath,\n      tags,\n    }),\n    name: input.name ?? tags.subcategory,\n    brand: input.brand ?? null,\n  };\n  const { error } = await supabase.from(\"items\").insert(row);\n  if (error) throw error;\n  revalidatePath(\"/closet\");\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Typecheck**\n\nRun: `npx tsc --noEmit`\nExpected: errors only in `components/capture/use-capture.ts` (Draft lacks `rotation`; fixed in Task 4).\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add app/closet/upload/actions.ts\ngit commit -m \"Capture: confirm can replace the cutout with its rotated version\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Confirm screen — preview the rotation, one button to fix it\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `components/capture/use-capture.ts` (Draft, capture(), save(), new `rotate()`)\n- Modify: `components/capture/confirm-form.tsx:33-64, 245-265` (prop + button)\n- Modify: `components/capture/capture-flow.tsx:31` and `components/capture/onboarding-capture.tsx:21-30` (pass `onRotate`)\n- Test: `components/capture/__tests__/` — check what exists there first (`ls`); if `use-capture` has a test, extend it, else the e2e in Task 5 is the test.\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: `rotateBlob`, `rotatedSize` (Task 2); `encodeCutout`, `encodeThumb`, `THUMB_MAX_PX` (existing); `confirmItem` with `rotated` (Task 3).\n- Produces: `Draft` gains `baseCutout: Blob` (the encoded cutout as uploaded, never rotated) and `rotation: Rotation`; `useCapture()` returns `rotate: () => Promise<void>`; `ConfirmForm` takes `onRotate: () => void`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Draft and capture()**\n\nIn `use-capture.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { rotateBlob } from \"@/lib/images/rotate\";\nimport { encodeCutout } from \"@/lib/images/encode\";\nimport { encodeThumb } from \"@/lib/images/thumb\";\nimport { THUMB_MAX_PX } from \"@/lib/images/options\";\nimport type { Rotation, Tags } from \"@/lib/ai/tagging-schema\";\n\nexport type Draft = {\n  imagePath: string;\n  cutoutPath: string;\n  thumbPath: string | null;\n  /** The uploaded cutout, unrotated. `cutoutUrl` always shows it turned by `rotation`. */\n  baseCutout: Blob;\n  rotation: Rotation;\n  cutoutUrl: string;\n  name: string;\n  brand: string;\n  tags: Tags;\n};\n```\n\nIn `capture()`, after `uploadAndTag` resolves:\n\n```ts\n      const shown = await rotateBlob(cutout, res.rotation);\n      setDraft({\n        imagePath: res.imagePath,\n        cutoutPath: res.cutoutPath,\n        thumbPath: res.thumbPath,\n        baseCutout: cutout,\n        rotation: res.rotation,\n        cutoutUrl: URL.createObjectURL(shown),\n        name: res.tags.subcategory,\n        brand: \"\",\n        tags: res.tags,\n      });\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: rotate()**\n\nAdd next to `updateDraft`:\n\n```ts\n  async function rotate() {\n    if (!draft) return;\n    const next = ((draft.rotation + 90) % 360) as Rotation;\n    const shown = await rotateBlob(draft.baseCutout, next);\n    setDraft((d) => (d ? { ...d, rotation: next, cutoutUrl: URL.createObjectURL(shown) } : d));\n  }\n```\n\nThe existing effect on `draft?.cutoutUrl` already revokes the previous object URL when it changes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: save()**\n\nBefore `confirmItem` in `save()`:\n\n```ts\n      let rotated = null;\n      if (draft.rotation !== 0) {\n        const { blob, mediaType } = await encodeCutout(await rotateBlob(draft.baseCutout, draft.rotation));\n        const thumb = await encodeThumb(blob, THUMB_MAX_PX);\n        rotated = {\n          cutoutB64: await blobToBase64(blob),\n          mediaType,\n          thumbB64: thumb ? await blobToBase64(thumb.blob) : null,\n          thumbMediaType: thumb?.mediaType ?? null,\n        };\n      }\n```\n\nand pass `rotated` in the `confirmItem({...})` call. Return `rotate` from the hook alongside `updateDraft`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: The button**\n\nIn `confirm-form.tsx`: import `RotateCw` from `lucide-react`; add `onRotate: () => void` to the props (type and destructuring). In the action row, between Retake and \"Add to closet\":\n\n```tsx\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          onClick={onRotate}\n          disabled={saving}\n          aria-label=\"Rotate\"\n          className=\"grid h-[54px] w-14 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-[14px] bg-surface-2 text-muted-foreground shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--hairline-6)] disabled:opacity-60\"\n        >\n          <RotateCw size={19} />\n        </button>\n```\n\nPass `onRotate={cap.rotate}` in `capture-flow.tsx` and `onboarding-capture.tsx`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Typecheck, lint, unit tests**\n\nRun: `npx tsc --noEmit && npm run lint && npm run test:run`\nExpected: all green.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add components/capture\ngit commit -m \"Capture: show the model's rotation on the confirm screen, one tap to correct it\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: e2e — the button turns the cutout, and the saved item is upright\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `e2e/capture-rotate.spec.ts`\n- Modify: `e2e/capture-exif.spec.ts` (already written; commit it here with its fixture `e2e/fixtures/garment-exif8.jpg`)\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: the confirm screen's `button[aria-label=\"Rotate\"]`, `.surface-stage img`; `e2e/helpers.ts` `admin()` and `testUserId()`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the spec**\n\n```ts\nimport { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\";\nimport { admin, testUserId } from \"./helpers\";\n\ntest.use({ storageState: \"e2e/.auth/state.json\" });\n\nasync function shownSize(page: import(\"@playwright/test\").Page) {\n  const img = page.locator(\".surface-stage img\").first();\n  await expect(img).toBeVisible({ timeout: 90_000 });\n  return img.evaluate(async (el: HTMLImageElement) => {\n    const bmp = await createImageBitmap(await (await fetch(el.src)).blob());\n    return { w: bmp.width, h: bmp.height };\n  });\n}\n\ntest(\"Rotate turns the preview a quarter turn and the saved cutout is stored turned\", async ({ page }) => {\n  test.setTimeout(180_000);\n  await page.goto(\"/closet/upload\");\n  await page.locator('input[type=\"file\"]').setInputFiles(\"e2e/fixtures/garment.jpg\");\n  const before = await shownSize(page); // the stub answers rotation 0, so this is the upload as-is\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Rotate\" }).click();\n  await expect.poll(async () => (await shownSize(page)).w).toBe(before.h);\n  expect(await shownSize(page)).toEqual({ w: before.h, h: before.w });\n\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Add to closet\" }).click();\n  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/closet/);\n\n  // The stored cutout is the turned one — not a CSS transform on the preview.\n  const db = admin();\n  const uid = await testUserId();\n  const { data: rows } = await db\n    .from(\"items\").select(\"id, cutout_url\").eq(\"user_id\", uid).order(\"created_at\", { ascending: false }).limit(1);\n  const row = rows![0];\n  const { data: blob } = await db.storage.from(\"wardrobe\").download(row.cutout_url);\n  const size = await page.evaluate(async (b64: string) => {\n    const bmp = await createImageBitmap(await (await fetch(`data:image/webp;base64,${b64}`)).blob());\n    return { w: bmp.width, h: bmp.height };\n  }, Buffer.from(await blob!.arrayBuffer()).toString(\"base64\"));\n  expect(size).toEqual({ w: before.h, h: before.w });\n\n  // Mutate, then put it back.\n  await db.storage.from(\"wardrobe\").remove([row.cutout_url, row.cutout_url.replace(/cutout\\.\\w+$/, \"original.jpg\")]);\n  await db.from(\"items\").delete().eq(\"id\", row.id);\n});\n```\n\nIf the closet redirect after save differs (read `components/capture/capture-flow.tsx` for what `onSaved` does), assert on that instead of the URL.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run the capture specs**\n\nRun: `set -a; source .env.local; set +a; npx playwright test e2e/capture*.spec.ts`\nExpected: 3 passed. If `download()` returns a blob whose type is PNG (WebP unsupported in the run), decode with `data:image/png` — or read the `Content-Type` from the row's extension.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add e2e/capture-rotate.spec.ts e2e/capture-exif.spec.ts e2e/fixtures/garment-exif8.jpg\ngit commit -m \"e2e: EXIF orientation and the Rotate button, through the real pipeline\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: Docs, review, PR\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `CLAUDE.md` (\"How the core flows actually work\" → Capture bullet: one sentence that the model also answers `rotation`, baked into the stored cutout at confirm)\n- Modify: `docs/superpowers/plans/roadmap-2026-09-14.md` (mark rotation done; add the fal.ai flag item: \"Cutout → fal.ai BiRefNet v2 ($0.0008/compute-s ≈ $0.001–0.002/image) behind a feature flag. Trigger: tag-correction rate on the confirm screen rises, or cutout complaints. Measured 2026-09-16: BiRefNet lite in-browser needs 1.3 GB WASM heap at 512 px — not shippable on phones.\")\n- Modify: `docs/STATE.md` TL;DR (branch, PR, the bake-off conclusion)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Full branch review** — mutation sweep: for each of `rotateRGBA` (swap the 90/270 formulas), `parseTaggingResponse` (drop the default 0), `confirmItem` (skip the upsert), `rotate()` (forget the `% 360`), make the mutation, run the relevant tests, confirm red, revert. A survivor is a finding — add the test.\n- [ ] **Step 2: `npm run build && npm run insights`** — routes untouched, but the capture components are in `/closet/upload` and onboarding.\n- [ ] **Step 3: Commit docs, push, open PR** into `develop` with the review table. Do NOT merge.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":311787,"output_tokens":11401,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":573,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11401,"cache_read_input_tokens":311787,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":573},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BkH4YerR33rp2t51as32Nm":{"file_path":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck/docs/superpowers/plans/todo/2026-09-16-cutout-rotation.md","content":"# Cutout Rotation Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** A garment photographed sideways or upside down ends up stored upright — Haiku drafts the rotation, the confirm screen shows it applied, and one button lets the user correct it before saving.\n\n**Architecture:** Rotation is NOT a tag and NOT a DB column: it is baked into the stored cutout and thumbnail at confirm time, so every reader (closet grid, flat-lay, Haiku re-tagging, share cards) sees an upright item with no per-view work. The model returns `rotation` (degrees clockwise: 0/90/180/270) alongside the tags because \"which way is up\" is semantic (a belt lying flat IS upright; trousers lying flat are not) — a geometric rule cannot decide it. The client keeps the uploaded cutout as the base, previews `rotate(base, rotation)`, and on save re-encodes and upserts the rotated cutout + thumb over the same storage paths. The original photo is never rotated (it is the photo).\n\n**Tech Stack:** Zod 4 + Anthropic structured outputs (`lib/ai/tagging-schema.ts`), canvas rotation on the client (`lib/images/`), Supabase Storage upsert in the existing Server Actions, Playwright WebKit e2e.\n\n**Spec:** This document (decided in conversation 2026-09-16; EXIF orientation was verified to already work end-to-end — `e2e/capture-exif.spec.ts`).\n\n## Global Constraints\n\n- Branch `feat/cutout-rotation` from `develop`; PR into `develop`. Never merge without an explicit go.\n- Full branch mutation review before push (memory: full-branch-review-before-pr).\n- Few code comments: one note per surprising decision.\n- `Test assets/` is never committed; e2e fixtures are the drawn `e2e/fixtures/garment*.jpg`.\n- `npm run test:run`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build` green; e2e for capture specs green (`set -a; source .env.local; set +a; npx playwright test e2e/capture*.spec.ts`).\n- Structured-output schemas go through `forStructuredOutput()`; no validation keywords.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Model returns `rotation`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `lib/ai/tagging-schema.ts` (after `export type Tags`, and `taggingJsonSchema`)\n- Modify: `lib/ai/parse-tags.ts:7-20`\n- Modify: `lib/ai/tag-item.ts:26-57`\n- Modify: `lib/ai/tagging-prompt.ts` (append a `rotation` paragraph)\n- Test: `lib/ai/__tests__/tagging-schema.test.ts`, `lib/ai/__tests__/parse-tags.test.ts`, `lib/ai/__tests__/tag-item-prompt.test.ts`\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Produces: `export const ROTATIONS = [0, 90, 180, 270] as const; export type Rotation = 0 | 90 | 180 | 270; export const RotationSchema`; `export function parseTaggingResponse(text: string): { tags: Tags; rotation: Rotation }`; `tagItem()` now resolves to `{ tags: Tags; rotation: Rotation }`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests**\n\nAppend to `lib/ai/__tests__/tagging-schema.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { RotationSchema, ROTATIONS, taggingJsonSchema } from \"../tagging-schema\";\n\ntest(\"rotation is one of four clockwise quarter turns\", () => {\n  for (const r of ROTATIONS) expect(RotationSchema.parse(r)).toBe(r);\n  expect(() => RotationSchema.parse(45)).toThrow();\n  expect(() => RotationSchema.parse(\"90\")).toThrow();\n});\n\ntest(\"the model is asked for rotation, as an enum of numbers\", () => {\n  const props = (taggingJsonSchema as { properties: Record<string, unknown> }).properties;\n  expect(props.rotation).toEqual({ type: \"number\", enum: [0, 90, 180, 270] });\n  expect((taggingJsonSchema as { required: string[] }).required).toContain(\"rotation\");\n});\n```\n\nAppend to `lib/ai/__tests__/parse-tags.test.ts` (reuse the file's existing valid-tags JSON fixture — call it `valid` below; if the file names it differently, use that name):\n\n```ts\nimport { parseTaggingResponse } from \"../parse-tags\";\n\ntest(\"parseTaggingResponse splits rotation from the tags\", () => {\n  const { tags, rotation } = parseTaggingResponse(JSON.stringify({ ...valid, rotation: 90 }));\n  expect(rotation).toBe(90);\n  expect(\"rotation\" in tags).toBe(false);\n});\n\ntest(\"a response without rotation is upright\", () => {\n  expect(parseTaggingResponse(JSON.stringify(valid)).rotation).toBe(0);\n});\n```\n\nAppend to `lib/ai/__tests__/tag-item-prompt.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\ntest(\"the prompt defines rotation as clockwise quarter turns and names the flat-lay exceptions\", () => {\n  expect(PROMPT).toContain(\"rotation\");\n  expect(PROMPT).toContain(\"clockwise\");\n  for (const r of [\"0\", \"90\", \"180\", \"270\"]) expect(PROMPT).toContain(r);\n  expect(PROMPT.toLowerCase()).toContain(\"belt\");\n});\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run them to see them fail**\n\nRun: `npx vitest run lib/ai`\nExpected: FAIL — `RotationSchema`/`parseTaggingResponse` not exported; prompt lacks \"rotation\".\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Schema**\n\nIn `lib/ai/tagging-schema.ts`, after `export type Tags = z.infer<typeof TagSchema>;`:\n\n```ts\n/**\n * Degrees CLOCKWISE to turn the photo so the item is upright as worn. Not a\n * tag: it is applied to the stored cutout at confirm time and never persisted.\n */\nexport const ROTATIONS = [0, 90, 180, 270] as const;\nexport type Rotation = (typeof ROTATIONS)[number];\nexport const RotationSchema = z.union([z.literal(0), z.literal(90), z.literal(180), z.literal(270)]);\n\n/** What the model answers: every tag a photo can settle, plus which way is up. */\nexport const TaggingResponseSchema = TagSchema.omit({ fit_source: true }).extend({\n  rotation: RotationSchema,\n});\n```\n\nReplace the `taggingJsonSchema` definition with:\n\n```ts\nexport const taggingJsonSchema = forStructuredOutput(\n  z.toJSONSchema(TaggingResponseSchema),\n) as Record<string, unknown>;\n```\n\nCheck what Zod 4 emits for the literal union: run `node -e 'const {z}=require(\"zod\");console.log(JSON.stringify(z.toJSONSchema(z.union([z.literal(0),z.literal(90),z.literal(180),z.literal(270)]))))'`. If it emits `anyOf` of `const`s instead of `{type:\"number\",enum:[...]}`, replace `RotationSchema` with `z.literal([0, 90, 180, 270])` (Zod 4 multi-value literal) and re-check — the test pins the enum shape because Anthropic's structured outputs accept `enum`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Parser**\n\nIn `lib/ai/parse-tags.ts`, keep `parseTagText` (tests and fixtures use it) and add:\n\n```ts\nimport { RotationSchema, TagSchema, WEARABLE_CATEGORIES, type Rotation, type Tags } from \"./tagging-schema\";\n\nexport function parseTaggingResponse(text: string): { tags: Tags; rotation: Rotation } {\n  let json: unknown;\n  try {\n    json = JSON.parse(text);\n  } catch {\n    throw new Error(\"Tagging response was not JSON\");\n  }\n  const { rotation, ...rest } = json as Record<string, unknown>;\n  return {\n    tags: TagSchema.parse({ fit_source: null, ...rest }),\n    rotation: rotation === undefined ? 0 : RotationSchema.parse(rotation),\n  };\n}\n```\n\nand make `parseTagText` delegate: `export function parseTagText(text: string): Tags { return parseTaggingResponse(text).tags; }`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: tagItem and the stub**\n\nIn `lib/ai/tag-item.ts`: import `parseTaggingResponse` instead of `parseTagText`; `stubbedTags()` returns `parseTaggingResponse(JSON.stringify({ ...same fields..., rotation: 0 }))`; `tagItem` returns `parseTaggingResponse(text)`. Update the trailing comment to \"validated draft tags + rotation\".\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Prompt**\n\nAppend to `PROMPT` in `lib/ai/tagging-prompt.ts`, before the closing backtick:\n\n```\nrotation — degrees CLOCKWISE to turn the photo so the item is upright as it is worn or \\\ncarried: 0, 90, 180 or 270. Upright means collar, waistband, hood or bag opening at the top and \\\nshoes standing on their soles. Items that are laid flat lengthways — a belt, a chain, a tie, a \\\nscarf, a watch strap — are upright at 0 when they run left to right. Answer 0 when unsure.\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the tests**\n\nRun: `npx vitest run lib/ai && npx tsc --noEmit`\nExpected: PASS; tsc reports `app/closet/upload/actions.ts` because `tagItem` now returns an object (fixed in Task 3) — that is the only error.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add lib/ai\ngit commit -m \"Tagging: the model answers which way is up\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Rotate a cutout on the client\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `lib/images/rotate.ts`\n- Test: `lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts`\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Produces: `rotatedSize(w, h, rotation): { width, height }`, `rotateRGBA(data: Uint8ClampedArray, width, height, rotation): { data: Uint8ClampedArray; width; height }` (pure), `rotateBlob(source: Blob, rotation: Rotation): Promise<Blob>` (browser; returns a PNG, alpha preserved; `rotation === 0` returns `source` untouched).\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests**\n\n`lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { rotateRGBA, rotatedSize } from \"../rotate\";\n\n// 2×1 image: red pixel left, blue pixel right.\nconst px = (r: number, g: number, b: number, a = 255) => [r, g, b, a];\nconst src = new Uint8ClampedArray([...px(255, 0, 0), ...px(0, 0, 255)]);\n\ntest(\"0 is identity\", () => {\n  const out = rotateRGBA(src, 2, 1, 0);\n  expect([out.width, out.height]).toEqual([2, 1]);\n  expect(Array.from(out.data)).toEqual(Array.from(src));\n});\n\ntest(\"90 clockwise puts the left pixel on top\", () => {\n  const out = rotateRGBA(src, 2, 1, 90);\n  expect([out.width, out.height]).toEqual([1, 2]);\n  expect(Array.from(out.data)).toEqual([...px(255, 0, 0), ...px(0, 0, 255)]);\n});\n\ntest(\"180 mirrors both axes\", () => {\n  const out = rotateRGBA(src, 2, 1, 180);\n  expect([out.width, out.height]).toEqual([2, 1]);\n  expect(Array.from(out.data)).toEqual([...px(0, 0, 255), ...px(255, 0, 0)]);\n});\n\ntest(\"270 clockwise puts the right pixel on top\", () => {\n  const out = rotateRGBA(src, 2, 1, 270);\n  expect([out.width, out.height]).toEqual([1, 2]);\n  expect(Array.from(out.data)).toEqual([...px(0, 0, 255), ...px(255, 0, 0)]);\n});\n\ntest(\"alpha survives\", () => {\n  const t = new Uint8ClampedArray([...px(1, 2, 3, 0), ...px(4, 5, 6, 128)]);\n  expect(Array.from(rotateRGBA(t, 2, 1, 90).data)).toEqual([...px(1, 2, 3, 0), ...px(4, 5, 6, 128)]);\n});\n\ntest(\"rotatedSize swaps on quarter turns only\", () => {\n  expect(rotatedSize(640, 800, 90)).toEqual({ width: 800, height: 640 });\n  expect(rotatedSize(640, 800, 180)).toEqual({ width: 640, height: 800 });\n});\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run to see them fail**\n\nRun: `npx vitest run lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL — module not found.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement**\n\n`lib/images/rotate.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { Rotation } from \"@/lib/ai/tagging-schema\";\n\nexport function rotatedSize(width: number, height: number, rotation: Rotation) {\n  return rotation % 180 === 0 ? { width, height } : { width: height, height: width };\n}\n\n/** Quarter-turn rotation of RGBA pixels, clockwise. Exact: no resampling. */\nexport function rotateRGBA(data: Uint8ClampedArray, width: number, height: number, rotation: Rotation) {\n  if (rotation === 0) return { data, width, height };\n  const { width: w2, height: h2 } = rotatedSize(width, height, rotation);\n  const out = new Uint8ClampedArray(data.length);\n  for (let y = 0; y < height; y++) {\n    for (let x = 0; x < width; x++) {\n      let nx: number, ny: number;\n      if (rotation === 90) { nx = height - 1 - y; ny = x; }\n      else if (rotation === 180) { nx = width - 1 - x; ny = height - 1 - y; }\n      else { nx = y; ny = width - 1 - x; }\n      const s = (y * width + x) * 4, d = (ny * w2 + nx) * 4;\n      out[d] = data[s]; out[d + 1] = data[s + 1]; out[d + 2] = data[s + 2]; out[d + 3] = data[s + 3];\n    }\n  }\n  return { data: out, width: w2, height: h2 };\n}\n\n/** Browser-only. Returns a PNG so alpha and pixels are untouched; encode afterwards. */\nexport async function rotateBlob(source: Blob, rotation: Rotation): Promise<Blob> {\n  if (rotation === 0) return source;\n  const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(source);\n  const canvas = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n  canvas.width = bitmap.width;\n  canvas.height = bitmap.height;\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n  if (!ctx) throw new Error(\"Canvas unavailable\");\n  ctx.drawImage(bitmap, 0, 0);\n  bitmap.close?.();\n  const src = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  const r = rotateRGBA(src.data, src.width, src.height, rotation);\n  canvas.width = r.width;\n  canvas.height = r.height;\n  ctx.putImageData(new ImageData(r.data, r.width, r.height), 0, 0);\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) =>\n    canvas.toBlob((b) => (b ? resolve(b) : reject(new Error(\"Rotate failed\"))), \"image/png\"),\n  );\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run the tests**\n\nRun: `npx vitest run lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts`\nExpected: PASS (6 tests).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add lib/images/rotate.ts lib/images/__tests__/rotate.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"Images: exact quarter-turn rotation of a cutout\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Server Actions carry rotation and accept the rotated blobs\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `app/closet/upload/actions.ts:68-75` (uploadAndTag return) and `:78-107` (confirmItem)\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: `tagItem() → { tags, rotation }` (Task 1); `cutoutFilename`, `thumbFilename` (existing).\n- Produces: `uploadAndTag` returns `{ itemId, imagePath, cutoutPath, thumbPath, tags, rotation }`; `confirmItem(input)` gains optional `rotated?: { cutoutB64: string; mediaType: CutoutMediaType; thumbB64: string | null; thumbMediaType: ThumbMediaType | null }` and returns nothing. When `rotated` is present the cutout and thumb at the draft's paths are REPLACED (upsert, same folder; filenames follow the media type actually produced), and the row is inserted with the resulting paths.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: uploadAndTag**\n\nReplace the tail of `uploadAndTag`:\n\n```ts\n  const { tags, rotation } = await tagItem(form.cutoutB64, form.mediaType);\n  return {\n    itemId,\n    imagePath: `${base}/original.jpg`,\n    cutoutPath: `${base}/${cutoutName}`,\n    thumbPath,\n    tags,\n    rotation,\n  };\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: confirmItem**\n\nReplace `confirmItem` with:\n\n```ts\n// Re-validate the (possibly user-edited) tags and insert the item. When the user\n// rotated the cutout, the rotated blobs replace the uploaded ones first, so the\n// row only ever points at upright images.\nexport async function confirmItem(input: {\n  imagePath: string;\n  cutoutPath: string;\n  thumbPath?: string | null;\n  name?: string | null;\n  brand?: string | null;\n  tags: unknown;\n  rotated?: {\n    cutoutB64: string;\n    mediaType: CutoutMediaType;\n    thumbB64: string | null;\n    thumbMediaType: ThumbMediaType | null;\n  } | null;\n}) {\n  const supabase = await createClient();\n  const {\n    data: { user },\n  } = await supabase.auth.getUser();\n  if (!user) throw new Error(\"Not authenticated\");\n\n  let cutoutPath = input.cutoutPath;\n  let thumbPath = input.thumbPath ?? null;\n  if (input.rotated) {\n    // Same defence as discardDraft: client-supplied paths, checked against the caller.\n    if (!cutoutPath.startsWith(`${user.id}/`)) throw new Error(\"Not your upload\");\n    const base = cutoutPath.slice(0, cutoutPath.lastIndexOf(\"/\"));\n    const nextCutout = `${base}/${cutoutFilename(input.rotated.mediaType)}`;\n    const { error } = await supabase.storage\n      .from(\"wardrobe\")\n      .upload(nextCutout, Buffer.from(input.rotated.cutoutB64, \"base64\"), {\n        contentType: input.rotated.mediaType,\n        upsert: true,\n      });\n    if (error) throw error;\n    const stale = [cutoutPath !== nextCutout ? cutoutPath : null];\n    cutoutPath = nextCutout;\n\n    let nextThumb: string | null = null;\n    if (input.rotated.thumbB64 && input.rotated.thumbMediaType) {\n      nextThumb = `${base}/${thumbFilename(input.rotated.thumbMediaType)}`;\n      const { error: thumbError } = await supabase.storage\n        .from(\"wardrobe\")\n        .upload(nextThumb, Buffer.from(input.rotated.thumbB64, \"base64\"), {\n          contentType: input.rotated.thumbMediaType,\n          upsert: true,\n        });\n      if (thumbError) nextThumb = null;\n    }\n    if (thumbPath && thumbPath !== nextThumb) stale.push(thumbPath);\n    thumbPath = nextThumb;\n    const remove = stale.filter((p): p is string => !!p);\n    if (remove.length) await supabase.storage.from(\"wardrobe\").remove(remove);\n  }\n\n  const tags = TagSchema.parse(input.tags);\n  const row = {\n    ...tagsToItemRow({\n      userId: user.id,\n      imageUrl: input.imagePath,\n      cutoutUrl: cutoutPath,\n      thumbUrl: thumbPath,\n      tags,\n    }),\n    name: input.name ?? tags.subcategory,\n    brand: input.brand ?? null,\n  };\n  const { error } = await supabase.from(\"items\").insert(row);\n  if (error) throw error;\n  revalidatePath(\"/closet\");\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Typecheck**\n\nRun: `npx tsc --noEmit`\nExpected: errors only in `components/capture/use-capture.ts` (Draft lacks `rotation`; fixed in Task 4).\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add app/closet/upload/actions.ts\ngit commit -m \"Capture: confirm can replace the cutout with its rotated version\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Confirm screen — preview the rotation, one button to fix it\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `components/capture/use-capture.ts` (Draft, capture(), save(), new `rotate()`)\n- Modify: `components/capture/confirm-form.tsx:33-64, 245-265` (prop + button)\n- Modify: `components/capture/capture-flow.tsx:31` and `components/capture/onboarding-capture.tsx:21-30` (pass `onRotate`)\n- Test: `components/capture/__tests__/` — check what exists there first (`ls`); if `use-capture` has a test, extend it, else the e2e in Task 5 is the test.\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: `rotateBlob`, `rotatedSize` (Task 2); `encodeCutout`, `encodeThumb`, `THUMB_MAX_PX` (existing); `confirmItem` with `rotated` (Task 3).\n- Produces: `Draft` gains `baseCutout: Blob` (the encoded cutout as uploaded, never rotated) and `rotation: Rotation`; `useCapture()` returns `rotate: () => Promise<void>`; `ConfirmForm` takes `onRotate: () => void`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Draft and capture()**\n\nIn `use-capture.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { rotateBlob } from \"@/lib/images/rotate\";\nimport { encodeCutout } from \"@/lib/images/encode\";\nimport { encodeThumb } from \"@/lib/images/thumb\";\nimport { THUMB_MAX_PX } from \"@/lib/images/options\";\nimport type { Rotation, Tags } from \"@/lib/ai/tagging-schema\";\n\nexport type Draft = {\n  imagePath: string;\n  cutoutPath: string;\n  thumbPath: string | null;\n  /** The uploaded cutout, unrotated. `cutoutUrl` always shows it turned by `rotation`. */\n  baseCutout: Blob;\n  rotation: Rotation;\n  cutoutUrl: string;\n  name: string;\n  brand: string;\n  tags: Tags;\n};\n```\n\nIn `capture()`, after `uploadAndTag` resolves:\n\n```ts\n      const shown = await rotateBlob(cutout, res.rotation);\n      setDraft({\n        imagePath: res.imagePath,\n        cutoutPath: res.cutoutPath,\n        thumbPath: res.thumbPath,\n        baseCutout: cutout,\n        rotation: res.rotation,\n        cutoutUrl: URL.createObjectURL(shown),\n        name: res.tags.subcategory,\n        brand: \"\",\n        tags: res.tags,\n      });\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: rotate()**\n\nAdd next to `updateDraft`:\n\n```ts\n  async function rotate() {\n    if (!draft) return;\n    const next = ((draft.rotation + 90) % 360) as Rotation;\n    const shown = await rotateBlob(draft.baseCutout, next);\n    setDraft((d) => (d ? { ...d, rotation: next, cutoutUrl: URL.createObjectURL(shown) } : d));\n  }\n```\n\nThe existing effect on `draft?.cutoutUrl` already revokes the previous object URL when it changes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: save()**\n\nBefore `confirmItem` in `save()`:\n\n```ts\n      let rotated = null;\n      if (draft.rotation !== 0) {\n        const { blob, mediaType } = await encodeCutout(await rotateBlob(draft.baseCutout, draft.rotation));\n        const thumb = await encodeThumb(blob, THUMB_MAX_PX);\n        rotated = {\n          cutoutB64: await blobToBase64(blob),\n          mediaType,\n          thumbB64: thumb ? await blobToBase64(thumb.blob) : null,\n          thumbMediaType: thumb?.mediaType ?? null,\n        };\n      }\n```\n\nand pass `rotated` in the `confirmItem({...})` call. Return `rotate` from the hook alongside `updateDraft`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: The button**\n\nIn `confirm-form.tsx`: import `RotateCw` from