t":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-rotation","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
{"parentUuid":"786baf9d-ec13-4016-9402-201bd0d0f3d9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31ebe121-f5a7-430a-9ee3-197a3ed7d39c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NadPNkqhN28Wr5xzHvK4KG","type":"tool_result","content":"# Roadmap — the one list. Agreed 2026-09-14, after 0.2.0 shipped.\n\n_Status 2026-09-16. ✅ = merged to develop. 🟡 = PR open. Everything else is not started._\n\n**Done since 0.2.0:** A · B · L1 (stage 0) · L2 · O6 · the CI trigger · the artefact clean-up.\n**Open PRs:** #83 (O2). **Next up:** L1b, then the owner decides.\n\nEverything open, from the owner's new asks, the `todo/` and `scoping/` queues,\nthe styling backlog, and memory. If it is not here it is not planned.\n⚠️ Order is a proposal until the owner confirms. ❓ = needs a decision first.\n\n---\n**L1b. ⏭ NEXT — Cutout model updates 1 and 2 (owner, 2026-09-16: \"don't forget\").**\nStage 0 (the swap, #80) is on develop with its parity reference committed. Two\nrefinements follow, each measured on the same 34 photos, with one table at the end\nshowing every image at stage 0 → 1 → 2 so the owner can see it got better:\n  1. **Guided-filter mask refinement** — the 320 px mask snapped to the full-resolution\n     photo's real edges (the image as guide). Targets the two known failures: the chain\n     bracelet's filled loop and the background leak between trouser legs. ~50 lines on\n     top of `segmentMask`, a few ms, no new download.\n  2. **Zoom pass** — bounding box from the first mask, crop, run u2netp again at 320 on\n     the crop so thin structures are effectively at higher resolution WITHOUT breaking\n     the model's scale assumptions (which is why 512/640 failed). One extra ~0.3 s.\n  Acceptance: `run.mjs --check` shows no regression on any image, and the two failures\n  improve. Reference = the visually correct one of {@imgly, ours} per image, chosen by\n  eye on the contact sheet and recorded. If a refinement helps nothing, it does not\n  ship — the harness decides, not the hope.\n\n**L2. ✅ Legal pages (#78, #79 guard fix) — DONE except the owner checklist below.** (#9 + #3): `/privacy`, `/terms`, footer links, a cookie\nnotice. Auth cookies are strictly necessary — a consent MANAGER only matters\nthe day analytics is added. Stripe requires the URLs. Lawyer reads the text.\n14:## 1.0 — the public, PAID release\n20:**L1. ✅ Background-removal — REBUILT (stage 0 merged in #80, 2026-09-16).**\n50:**L2. ✅ Legal pages (#78, #79 guard fix) — DONE except the owner checklist below.** (#9 + #3): `/privacy`, `/terms`, footer links, a cookie\n69:**L3. Stripe** — the rail for the tier that already exists.\n94:**L4. Self-serve account deletion.** Found while writing the privacy policy:\n102:**A. ✅ (#76)** \"Try another look\" is on the wrong page and colliding with the bottom\n105:**B. ✅ (#77)** Bag-echo inversion — a black bag beats the bag that echoes the trousers.\n110:**D. Batch upload** (#10). Pick many → queue → Web Worker processing while the\n113:**E. Share a look** (#6). Story image 1080×1920, square, public link. Was\n120:**P1. Real-photo capture testing** — deferred by the owner until the generator\n123:**P2. End-of-build design audit** — impeccable + design-taste-frontend across\n126:**P3. E2E coverage** — `todo/2026-08-19-e2e-foundation.md`; extend the\n131:## 1.1\n133:**F. Tomorrow's look** (#4). ❓ On rollover, does tomorrow's set become\n136:**G. Add from a link** (#5) — clothes and perfumes. Server fetches the URL,\n143:**H. Languages — German, Russian, Ukrainian** (#1). next-intl, extraction,\n147:**I. ❓ The quiz** (#2). (a) review what the six answers do to the generator,\n151:**J. Cutout backfill** — `todo/2026-07-22-cutout-backfill.md`. Re-encode\n154:**K. Passkeys** — CLAUDE.md Decision 1 promised \"its own scoped plan\". Face ID\n159:## Operations — raised by the owner 2026-09-16\n161:**O1. Database and Storage backups — decided: MANUAL for now (owner, 2026-09-16).** ⚠️ The Supabase org is on the\n177:**O2. 🟡 Legal-page visibility (#83, open).** `/privacy` and `/terms` are linked from the sign-in\n183:**O3. Sentry — use what is already wired, add three things.** Source maps upload is\n192:**O4. Doppler (owner has a Team Developer subscription).** Worth adopting: today secrets\n199:**O5. Analytics — where to look.** `@vercel/analytics` shipped in #78. ⚠️ It must be\n206:**O6. E2E in CI — done 2026-09-16 (#82).** The workflow existed but only fired for PRs\n211:## Styling backlog (discuss each before building — owner's standing rule)\n224:## Deferred by decision — re-confirm before touching\n235:## Housekeeping","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b7429d49-f60c-4980-b5b3-db6072ff71ef","timestamp":"2026-09-16T21:58:08.849Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Roadmap — the one list. Agreed 2026-09-14, after 0.2.0 shipped.\n\n_Status 2026-09-16. ✅ = merged to develop. 🟡 = PR open. Everything else is not started._\n\n**Done since 0.2.0:** A · B · L1 (stage 0) · L2 · O6 · the CI trigger · the artefact clean-up.\n**Open PRs:** #83 (O2). **Next up:** L1b, then the owner decides.\n\nEverything open, from the owner's new asks, the `todo/` and `scoping/` queues,\nthe styling backlog, and memory. If it is not here it is not planned.\n⚠️ Order is a proposal until the owner confirms. ❓ = needs a decision first.\n\n---\n**L1b. ⏭ NEXT — Cutout model updates 1 and 2 (owner, 2026-09-16: \"don't forget\").**\nStage 0 (the swap, #80) is on develop with its parity reference committed. Two\nrefinements follow, each measured on the same 34 photos, with one table at the end\nshowing every image at stage 0 → 1 → 2 so the owner can see it got better:\n  1. **Guided-filter mask refinement** — the 320 px mask snapped to the full-resolution\n     photo's real edges (the image as guide). Targets the two known failures: the chain\n     bracelet's filled loop and the background leak between trouser legs. ~50 lines on\n     top of `segmentMask`, a few ms, no new download.\n  2. **Zoom pass** — bounding box from the first mask, crop, run u2netp again at 320 on\n     the crop so thin structures are effectively at higher resolution WITHOUT breaking\n     the model's scale assumptions (which is why 512/640 failed). One extra ~0.3 s.\n  Acceptance: `run.mjs --check` shows no regression on any image, and the two failures\n  improve. Reference = the visually correct one of {@imgly, ours} per image, chosen by\n  eye on the contact sheet and recorded. If a refinement helps nothing, it does not\n  ship — the harness decides, not the hope.\n\n**L2. ✅ Legal pages (#78, #79 guard fix) — DONE except the owner checklist below.** (#9 + #3): `/privacy`, `/terms`, footer links, a cookie\nnotice. Auth cookies are strictly necessary — a consent MANAGER only matters\nthe day analytics is added. Stripe requires the URLs. Lawyer reads the text.\n14:## 1.0 — the public, PAID release\n20:**L1. ✅ Background-removal — REBUILT (stage 0 merged in #80, 2026-09-16).**\n50:**L2. ✅ Legal pages (#78, #79 guard fix) — DONE except the owner checklist below.** (#9 + #3): `/privacy`, `/terms`, footer links, a cookie\n69:**L3. Stripe** — the rail for the tier that already exists.\n94:**L4. Self-serve account deletion.** Found while writing the privacy policy:\n102:**A. ✅ (#76)** \"Try another look\" is on the wrong page and colliding with the bottom\n105:**B. ✅ (#77)** Bag-echo inversion — a black bag beats the bag that echoes the trousers.\n110:**D. Batch upload** (#10). Pick many → queue → Web Worker processing while the\n113:**E. Share a look** (#6). Story image 1080×1920, square, public link. Was\n120:**P1. Real-photo capture testing** — deferred by the owner until the generator\n123:**P2. End-of-build design audit** — impeccable + design-taste-frontend across\n126:**P3. E2E coverage** — `todo/2026-08-19-e2e-foundation.md`; extend the\n131:## 1.1\n133:**F. Tomorrow's look** (#4). ❓ On rollover, does tomorrow's set become\n136:**G. Add from a link** (#5) — clothes and perfumes. Server fetches the URL,\n143:**H. Languages — German, Russian, Ukrainian** (#1). next-intl, extraction,\n147:**I. ❓ The quiz** (#2). (a) review what the six answers do to the generator,\n151:**J. Cutout backfill** — `todo/2026-07-22-cutout-backfill.md`. Re-encode\n154:**K. Passkeys** — CLAUDE.md Decision 1 promised \"its own scoped plan\". Face ID\n159:## Operations — raised by the owner 2026-09-16\n161:**O1. Database and Storage backups — decided: MANUAL for now (owner, 2026-09-16).** ⚠️ The Supabase org is on the\n177:**O2. 🟡 Legal-page visibility (#83, open).** `/privacy` and `/terms` are linked from the sign-in\n183:**O3. Sentry — use what is already wired, add three things.** Source maps upload is\n192:**O4. Doppler (owner has a Team Developer subscription).** Worth adopting: today secrets\n199:**O5. Analytics — where to look.** `@vercel/analytics` shipped in #78. ⚠️ It must be\n206:**O6. E2E in CI — done 2026-09-16 (#82).** The workflow existed but only fired for PRs\n211:## Styling backlog (discuss each before building — owner's standing rule)\n224:## Deferred by decision — re-confirm before touching\n235:## Housekeeping","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"786baf9d-ec13-4016-9402-201bd0d0f3d9","session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-rotation","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
