{"parentUuid":"6e754166-c584-472f-b86e-1a67e864d7c0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14911378 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"47ddedc1-88d5-4d32-aa54-5d81685cb1c4","timestamp":"2026-09-16T21:58:08.858Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14911378 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-rotation","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
{"parentUuid":"47ddedc1-88d5-4d32-aa54-5d81685cb1c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf7sGSjCvGpWmsLAPTeGT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017rVPPne9GV9xJQt3LHC8sE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck; python3 - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/superpowers/plans/roadmap-2026-09-14.md\"; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"**Open PRs:** #83 (O2). **Next up:** L1b, then the owner decides.\",\n\"**Open PRs:** #83 (O2) · #84 (L1b sharpen + bake-off harness) · L1c rotation (this branch). **Next up:** the owner decides.\")\nold=s[s.index(\"**L1b. ⏭ NEXT — Cutout model updates 1 and 2\"):s.index(\"**L2. ✅ Legal pages\")]\nnew='''**L1b. 🟡 Cutout refinement (#84).** Sharpen shipped (10 under bar, worst 0.80 → measured on the 34).\nGuided filter and zoom were built, measured, and rejected (blur / no gain). Decided 2026-09-16.\n\n**L1c. 🟡 Rotation (branch `feat/cutout-rotation`).** Haiku answers `rotation` (0/90/180/270,\nclockwise) with the tags; the confirm screen previews it and a Rotate button corrects it; the\nrotated cutout + thumb REPLACE the stored ones at confirm, so every reader sees an upright item.\nEXIF orientation from a sideways phone was verified to already work (`e2e/capture-exif.spec.ts`).\n\n**L1d. 🚩 FLAG — cutout → fal.ai BiRefNet v2 (owner, 2026-09-16: \"make flag about fal.ai\").**\nThe bake-off (11 models, 34 photos, contact sheets in `scratch/`): BiRefNet (MIT) is the only\nclearly better cutout — crisp edges on real phone photos where u2netp is soft and haloed at full\nzoom; identical at closet-grid size. In-browser BiRefNet lite works (512 px, WASM, 1.1 s on an\nM-series Mac) but needs **1.3 GB of WASM heap** — the architecture's live activations, not a\nkernel bug — so it is not shippable on phones. fal.ai hosts it: `fal-ai/birefnet/v2`,\n**$0.0008 per compute-second ≈ $0.001–0.002 per image**, ~2–4 s round trip, no cold start.\n**Trigger to build:** tag-correction rate on the confirm screen rises, or users complain about\ncutouts. **Shape:** a feature flag in `lib/images/process.ts` — Server Action → fal → same\n`encodeCutout`/`encodeThumb` path; u2netp on-device stays as the fallback when the call fails.\nOne more processor in the privacy policy (US, like Anthropic). ~1 day.\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\n\np=\"CLAUDE.md\"; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"calls Haiku for a **draft** tag set. **No DB row is written yet** — the user reviews on a confirm\\n  screen, then `confirmItem` re-validates (`TagSchema.parse`) and inserts.\",\n\"calls Haiku for a **draft** tag set plus `rotation` (which way is up — semantic, so the model answers\\n  it). **No DB row is written yet** — the user reviews on a confirm screen (the cutout shown already\\n  turned, one button to correct), then `confirmItem` re-validates (`TagSchema.parse`), replaces the\\n  stored cutout + thumb with the rotated ones when turned, and inserts. Rotation is never a column.\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"rotation\" CLAUDE.md | head -3; git diff --stat","description":"Update roadmap and CLAUDE.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2091,"cache_read_input_tokens":359562,"output_tokens":1351,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2091,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1351,"cache_read_input_tokens":359562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2091,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2091},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017rVPPne9GV9xJQt3LHC8sE":{"command":"cd /Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck; python3 - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/superpowers/plans/roadmap-2026-09-14.md\"; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"**Open PRs:** #83 (O2). **Next up:** L1b, then the owner decides.\",\n\"**Open PRs:** #83 (O2) · #84 (L1b sharpen + bake-off harness) · L1c rotation (this branch). **Next up:** the owner decides.\")\nold=s[s.index(\"**L1b. ⏭ NEXT — Cutout model updates 1 and 2\"):s.index(\"**L2. ✅ Legal pages\")]\nnew='''**L1b. 🟡 Cutout refinement (#84).** Sharpen shipped (10 under bar, worst 0.80 → measured on the 34).\nGuided filter and zoom were built, measured, and rejected (blur / no gain). Decided 2026-09-16.\n\n**L1c. 🟡 Rotation (branch `feat/cutout-rotation`).** Haiku answers `rotation` (0/90/180/270,\nclockwise) with the tags; the confirm screen previews it and a Rotate button corrects it; the\nrotated cutout + thumb REPLACE the stored ones at confirm, so every reader sees an upright item.\nEXIF orientation from a sideways phone was verified to already work (`e2e/capture-exif.spec.ts`).\n\n**L1d. 🚩 FLAG — cutout → fal.ai BiRefNet v2 (owner, 2026-09-16: \"make flag about fal.ai\").**\nThe bake-off (11 models, 34 photos, contact sheets in `scratch/`): BiRefNet (MIT) is the only\nclearly better cutout — crisp edges on real phone photos where u2netp is soft and haloed at full\nzoom; identical at closet-grid size. In-browser BiRefNet lite works (512 px, WASM, 1.1 s on an\nM-series Mac) but needs **1.3 GB of WASM heap** — the architecture's live activations, not a\nkernel bug — so it is not shippable on phones. fal.ai hosts it: `fal-ai/birefnet/v2`,\n**$0.0008 per compute-second ≈ $0.001–0.002 per image**, ~2–4 s round trip, no cold start.\n**Trigger to build:** tag-correction rate on the confirm screen rises, or users complain about\ncutouts. **Shape:** a feature flag in `lib/images/process.ts` — Server Action → fal → same\n`encodeCutout`/`encodeThumb` path; u2netp on-device stays as the fallback when the call fails.\nOne more processor in the privacy policy (US, like Anthropic). ~1 day.\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\n\np=\"CLAUDE.md\"; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"calls Haiku for a **draft** tag set. **No DB row is written yet** — the user reviews on a confirm\\n  screen, then `confirmItem` re-validates (`TagSchema.parse`) and inserts.\",\n\"calls Haiku for a **draft** tag set plus `rotation` (which way is up — semantic, so the model answers\\n  it). **No DB row is written yet** — the user reviews on a confirm screen (the cutout shown already\\n  turned, one button to correct), then `confirmItem` re-validates (`TagSchema.parse`), replaces the\\n  stored cutout + thumb with the rotated ones when turned, and inserts. Rotation is never a column.\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"rotation\" CLAUDE.md | head -3; git diff --stat","description":"Update roadmap and CLAUDE.md"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf7sGPS1Hq4H3QP9jmFJk","attributionSkill":"superpowers:executing-plans","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"b26bda00-3619-47a2-806b-ea9475ac18ad","timestamp":"2026-09-16T21:58:26.971Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-rotation","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
