{"parentUuid":"b26bda00-3619-47a2-806b-ea9475ac18ad","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31ebe121-f5a7-430a-9ee3-197a3ed7d39c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017rVPPne9GV9xJQt3LHC8sE","type":"tool_result","content":"77:  calls Haiku for a **draft** tag set plus `rotation` (which way is up — semantic, so the model answers","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"acdfa812-43f0-4f46-8540-3b5a488bc7d3","timestamp":"2026-09-16T21:58:29.685Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"77:  calls Haiku for a **draft** tag set plus `rotation` (which way is up — semantic, so the model answers","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b26bda00-3619-47a2-806b-ea9475ac18ad","session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-rotation","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
{"parentUuid":"acdfa812-43f0-4f46-8540-3b5a488bc7d3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_017rVPPne9GV9xJQt3LHC8sE","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"_R=\"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\"; [ -z \"$_R\" ] && _R=\"$HOME/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/thedotmack/plugin\"; node \"$_R/scripts/bun-runner.js\" \"$_R/scripts/worker-service.cjs\" hook claude-code observation","durationMs":154},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5d0ce00c-57da-4f31-a1e7-afa03aaab19d","timestamp":"2026-09-16T21:58:29.685Z","session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-rotation","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
{"parentUuid":"5d0ce00c-57da-4f31-a1e7-afa03aaab19d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck/CLAUDE.md","snippet":"69\t\n70\t- **Supabase clients — three factories, don't mix them**: `lib/supabase/server.ts` (Server\n71\t  Components / Actions, via `cookies()`), `lib/supabase/client.ts` (browser), `lib/supabase/proxy.ts`\n72\t  (session refresh in `proxy.ts`). Every DB access relies on RLS = `auth.uid() = user_id`; there is no\n73\t  service-role bypass in app code.\n74\t- **Capture = two-phase, image work is client-side** (Decision 2/3): the browser runs\n75\t  `lib/images/process.ts` (compress → our own `onnxruntime-web` + u2netp background-removal in `lib/images/segment.ts`, **on-device, zero cost**),\n76\t  then `uploadAndTag` (Server Action) stores both blobs under `wardrobe/<user_id>/<item_id>/` and\n77\t  calls Haiku for a **draft** tag set plus `rotation` (which way is up — semantic, so the model answers\n78\t  it). **No DB row is written yet** — the user reviews on a confirm screen (the cutout shown already\n79\t  turned, one button to correct), then `confirmItem` re-validates (`TagSchema.parse`), replaces the\n80\t  stored cutout + thumb with the rotated ones when turned, and inserts. Rotation is never a column. Storage paths are private;\n81\t  the closet renders them via short-lived signed URLs (`lib/storage/signed.ts`).\n82\t- **AI tagging is schema-constrained, never prompt-and-parsed** (Decision 3): `lib/ai/tag-item.ts`\n83\t  sends the cutout to `claude-haiku-4-5` with `output_config.format` (json_schema). Keep the Zod\n84\t  schema, the JSON schema, and the DB row mapping in `lib/ai/` in sync.\n85\t\n86\t---\n87\t\n88\t## Tech stack (committed)"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1094749e-c4a6-4788-be9c-48bde86f4c39","timestamp":"2026-09-16T21:58:29.698Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck/CLAUDE.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n69\t\n70\t- **Supabase clients — three factories, don't mix them**: `lib/supabase/server.ts` (Server\n71\t  Components / Actions, via `cookies()`), `lib/supabase/client.ts` (browser), `lib/supabase/proxy.ts`\n72\t  (session refresh in `proxy.ts`). Every DB access relies on RLS = `auth.uid() = user_id`; there is no\n73\t  service-role bypass in app code.\n74\t- **Capture = two-phase, image work is client-side** (Decision 2/3): the browser runs\n75\t  `lib/images/process.ts` (compress → our own `onnxruntime-web` + u2netp background-removal in `lib/images/segment.ts`, **on-device, zero cost**),\n76\t  then `uploadAndTag` (Server Action) stores both blobs under `wardrobe/<user_id>/<item_id>/` and\n77\t  calls Haiku for a **draft** tag set plus `rotation` (which way is up — semantic, so the model answers\n78\t  it). **No DB row is written yet** — the user reviews on a confirm screen (the cutout shown already\n79\t  turned, one button to correct), then `confirmItem` re-validates (`TagSchema.parse`), replaces the\n80\t  stored cutout + thumb with the rotated ones when turned, and inserts. Rotation is never a column. Storage paths are private;\n81\t  the closet renders them via short-lived signed URLs (`lib/storage/signed.ts`).\n82\t- **AI tagging is schema-constrained, never prompt-and-parsed** (Decision 3): `lib/ai/tag-item.ts`\n83\t  sends the cutout to `claude-haiku-4-5` with `output_config.format` (json_schema). Keep the Zod\n84\t  schema, the JSON schema, and the DB row mapping in `lib/ai/` in sync.\n85\t\n86\t---\n87\t\n88\t## Tech stack (committed)\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"4608eecb-4caf-46b4-83e5-d59d81f329b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/1curafu/Desktop/Fitcheck/Fitcheck","sessionId":"8dbc8706-da4b-488c-b8be-7203d3d08172","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"feat/cutout-rotation","slug":"groovy-floating-penguin"}
